t["subzone:talondeep-path"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,267,21.684.0,35.211.0,48.194.0,36.211.0,46.198.0",["h"]="26eefb",["n"]="El Paso del Espolón",["s"]="El Paso del Espolón. El Paso del Espolón es un serpenteante túnel subterráneo que atraviesa la cordillera montañosa situada entre Vallefresno y Sierra Espolón. Desprovisto de criaturas hostiles o viajeros, sirve como un paso subterráneo natural y tranquilo que conecta el Lago Mystral con el Risco Cortaviento. Oculto bajo la escarpada cresta que separa Vallefresno y Sierra Espolón se encuentra El Paso del Espolón, una tranquila ruta subterránea. El paso une los bosques situados justo al oeste del Lago Mystral directamente con los confines noroccidentales del Risco Cortaviento. A diferencia de los peligrosos senderos de la superficie, acechados por depredadores y facciones enfrentadas, el interior del túnel permanece misteriosamente en calma, libre de bestias hostiles o campamentos, aunque plagado de recovecos serpenteantes, grietas y nichos naturales en la roca. En la superficie aún perduran los tenues vestigios de un antiguo camino exterior, lo que sugiere que antaño los viajeros escalaban los altos picos antes de que esta cueva protegida se convirtiera en la ruta predilecta a través de la piedra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Mining"]="The cavern's winding rock alcoves cut straight through the deep stone foundation of the mountain range, making it a natural landmark when navigating between mineral-rich Ashenvale and Stonetalon."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The tunnel connects southwestern Ashenvale to northeastern Stonetalon Mountains. Its northern entrance sits just west of Mystral Lake, while its southern mouth opens into the northwestern side of Windshear Crag.",["al"]={"where does talondeep path go","talondeep path connections","talondeep tunnel exits"},["q"]="Where does the Talondeep Path lead?"},{["a"]="No. The interior of the cavern is uniquely peaceful and completely barren of hostile monsters, beasts, or friendly NPCs, making it a safe passageway for travelers traversing the mountain divide.",["al"]={"is talondeep path safe","talondeep path mobs","talondeep path threats"},["q"]="Are there monsters or enemies inside the tunnel?"},{["a"]="Remnants of an overgrown surface road run along the mountain ridge directly above the cavern. It suggests an older, treacherous overland route across the crags predated the passage through the hollowed interior.",["al"]={"road above talondeep path","overland path stonetalon"},["q"]="What are the ruins above the cavern?"},{["a"]="Neither faction holds the tunnel. It is entirely unfortified and neutral wilderness, allowing safe foot passage for travelers of any allegiance moving between the contested forest and the mountains.",["al"]={"who controls talondeep path","talondeep path faction"},["q"]="Is Talondeep Path an Alliance or Horde tunnel?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","cave","mystral lake","stonetalon","talondeep","talondeep path","tunnel","windshear crag"},["n"]="Talondeep Path",["s"]="Talondeep Path is a winding underground tunnel boring through the mountain ridge between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains. Devoid of hostile creatures or travelers, it serves as a tranquil, natural subterranean passage connecting Mystral Lake to Windshear Crag.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Hidden beneath the rugged ridgeline separating Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains lies Talondeep Path, a quiet subterranean route. The passage links the forests just west of Mystral Lake directly to the northwestern reaches of Windshear Crag. Unlike the dangerous surface trails haunted by predators and warring factions, the tunnel interior remains eerily calm, free of hostile beasts or encampments, though riddled with twisting side pockets, crevices, and natural alcoves in the rock. Above ground, faint remnants of an ancient surface road still linger, hinting that travelers once scaled the high peaks before this sheltered cave became the preferred route through the stone.",["t"]="A Quiet Mountain Pass"}}}}}
t["subzone:talondeep-vale"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,256,18.502.0,32.183.0,54.208.0,49.174.0",["h"]="02da6d",["n"]="Vega del Espolón",["s"]="Vega del Espolón. Vega del Espolón es una hondonada boscosa y tranquila enclavada en la zona centro-sur de Vallefresno. Bordeando el Refugio Brisa de Plata, las Ruinas del Polvo Estelar y la entrada a Sierra Espolón, actúa como un dosel pacífico a través del cual los viajeros se desplazan por el sur de Kalimdor. Escondida bajo el denso dosel de la zona centro-sur de Vallefresno, Vega del Espolón sirve como encrucijada entre varios lugares emblemáticos. Está flanqueada por el Refugio Brisa de Plata al este, las inquietantes Ruinas del Polvo Estelar en las cercanías y la escarpada cuesta que conduce a Sierra Espolón. En la sombra de árboles ancestrales, el valle sigue siendo una extensión de bosque salvaje por la que transitan celadoras de los elfos de la noche, centinelas y caminantes de paso mientras se desplazan entre el corazón del bosque y los altos riscos más allá.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:NightElf"]="Nestled near the sacred waters of Mystral Lake and the Ruins of Stardust, these valley paths are familiar ground to the sentinels and wardens patrolling southern Ashenvale."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Talondeep Vale lies in south-central Ashenvale, nestled between Silverwind Refuge, the ancient Ruins of Stardust, and the southern mountain pass heading into the Stonetalon Mountains.",["al"]={"where is talondeep vale","talondeep vale location","how to find talondeep vale"},["q"]="Where is Talondeep Vale located?"},{["a"]="Following the trail through the vale leads travelers toward Talondeep Path, an ascent through the rugged heights connecting the woodlands of Ashenvale directly with the arid peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains.",["al"]={"path south talondeep vale","where does talondeep pass lead","road to stonetalon"},["q"]="Where does the path leading south through the vale go?"},{["a"]="The vale sits adjacent to Silverwind Refuge to the east, as well as the waterlogged Ruins of Stardust, where ancient night elven remnants still stand beneath the tree boughs.",["al"]={"landmarks near talondeep vale","what is near talondeep vale"},["q"]="What nearby landmarks should travelers watch for?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","ruins of stardust","silverwind refuge","stardust spire","talondeep pass","talondeep path","talondeep vale"},["n"]="Talondeep Vale",["s"]="Talondeep Vale is a quiet, forested hollow nestled in south-central Ashenvale. Bordering Silverwind Refuge, the Ruins of Stardust, and the gateway to the Stonetalon Mountains, it acts as a peaceful canopy through which travelers navigate southern Kalimdor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away beneath the dense canopy of south-central Ashenvale, Talondeep Vale serves as a crossroads between several landmark sites. It is framed by Silverwind Refuge to the east, the haunting Ruins of Stardust nearby, and the rugged rise leading up into the Stonetalon Mountains. Shaded by ancient trees, the valley remains an untamed tract of woodland through which night elf wardens, sentinels, and passing wanderers traverse as they move between the heart of the forest and the high crags beyond.",["t"]="A Sheltered Valley"}}}}}
t["subzone:tarren-mill"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,317,19.631.0,23.462.0,35.138.0,44.306.0,44.250.0,59.201.0",["h"]="0056ec",["n"]="Molino Tarren",["s"]="Molino Tarren. Molino Tarren es un asediado puesto de avanzada de los Renegados enclavado en los confines septentrionales de las Laderas de Trabalomas, al pie de las Montañas de Alterac. Antaño una pacífica aldea agrícola humana, ahora sirve como el bastión principal de la Horda en Trabalomas, enfrascado en un conflicto constante con la villa de Costasur de la Alianza al sur. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, Molino Tarren era un próspero municipio agrícola leal al Reino de Lordaeron. Durante la Segunda Guerra, cobró renombre cuando las fuerzas de la Alianza rescataron a arqueros altos elfos capturados de campamentos orcos cercanos, asegurando el pleno compromiso de Quel'Thalas con la Alianza de Lordaeron. Hoy en día, sin embargo, los habitantes vivos originales de la villa han desaparecido, reemplazados por los Renegados. La arquitectura del asentamiento se alza desgastada y deteriorada, sus campos están yermos y su viejo molino permanece en silencio mientras los nuevos ocupantes no-muertos fortifican el lugar contra las constantes amenazas de bestias montañosas, forajidos de la Hermandad y hostigadores de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Tarren Mill is your only major refuge in the Hillsbrad Foothills, offering a bat handler, supplies, and vital military support against encroaching Alliance forces from Southshore.",["race:Undead"]="Taking hold of Tarren Mill expands Queen Sylvanas's southern borders, turning a once-proud Lordaeron farming town into a strategic stronghold against the living."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tarren Mill is controlled entirely by the Forsaken and functions as the primary Horde questing hub and outpost in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",["al"]={"who owns tarren mill","is tarren mill horde or alliance","tarren mill faction"},["q"]="Who controls Tarren Mill right now?"},{["a"]="Tarren Mill represents the Forsaken and the Horde's southern reach in Lordaeron, while Southshore is the last major stronghold of the Alliance in the region. Their close proximity makes ongoing territorial warfare inevitable as both factions contest control of Hillsbrad's fertile land and strategic roads.",["al"]={"southshore vs tarren mill","why fight southshore","hillsbrad war"},["q"]="Why are Tarren Mill and Southshore fighting?"},{["a"]="It was a peaceful human farming and milling settlement of the Kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Second War, Alliance soldiers famously freed captive high elven archers near the town, securing Quel'Thalas's military pact with the Alliance of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"tarren mill history","who lived here before","tarren mill lore"},["q"]="What was Tarren Mill like before the plague?"},{["a"]="Beyond Southshore's forces, Tarren Mill must contend with local bandits of the Syndicate, highland yetis and ogres descending from the Alterac peaks, and fierce mountain wildlife roaming the foothills.",["al"]={"tarren mill enemies","local dangers hillsbrad"},["q"]="What threats exist around Tarren Mill besides the Alliance?"}},["kw"]={"alterac","forsaken","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","lordaeron","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},["n"]="Tarren Mill",["s"]="Tarren Mill is a beleaguered Forsaken outpost nestled in the northern reaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills beneath the Alterac Mountains. Once a peaceful human farming village, it now serves as the primary bastion of the Horde in Hillsbrad, locked in constant conflict with the Alliance town of Southshore to the south.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, Tarren Mill was a thriving agricultural township loyal to the Kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Second War, it earned renown when Alliance forces rescued captured high elven archers from nearby orc encampments, securing Quel'Thalas's full commitment to the Alliance of Lordaeron. Today, however, the town's original living inhabitants are gone, replaced by the Forsaken. The town's architecture stands weathered and decayed, its fields barren, and its old mill silent as the new undead occupants fortify the settlement against constant threats from mountain beasts, Syndicate outlaws, and Alliance skirmishers.",["t"]="From Grain to Grave"},{["b"]="Tarren Mill functions as the Horde's vital forward operations base in the region. Directly opposed to the Alliance port of Southshore, the road between the two settlements has devolved into an open warzone. Horde travelers use Tarren Mill to push back against the human farmers and soldiers occupying Hillsbrad, coordinate strikes against dwarven excavators at Dun Garok, and secure the treacherous roads leading up into the snowy crags of the Alterac Mountains.",["t"]="Front Line of Hillsbrad"}}}}}
t["subzone:temple-gardens"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,273,26.462.0,21.431.0,47.289.0,36.136.0,39.141.0,46.219.0",["h"]="5714ef",["n"]="Los Jardines del Templo",["s"]="Los Jardines del Templo. Los Jardines del Templo forman el corazón tranquilo y acuático de Darnassus, rodeando pequeños islotes justo al norte del Templo de la Luna. Decorado con puentes y una flora impoluta, el distrito alberga el banco de la ciudad y el místico portal arbóreo que conduce a la base de Teldrassil. Extendiéndose sobre las aguas del centro de Darnassus, Los Jardines del Templo sirven como cruce de caminos de la capital de los elfos de la noche. Puentes de madera conectan sus islotes ajardinados con el Enclave Cenarion al norte, las bulliciosas terrazas al este y el gran santuario del Templo de la Luna al sur. Los elfos de la noche moldean cuidadosamente las aguas y el frondoso follaje del distrito, creando una atmósfera serena que ofrece descanso tanto a viajeros como a sacerdotisas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Any visitor sailing in through the docks must step through the Rut'theran portal into these tranquil waters to access the rest of the city.",["race:NightElf"]="The gardens represent the harmonious blend of wilderness and civic architecture that defines Darnassian culture, offering peace for reflection amidst administrative daily life."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The glowing tree portal on the western edge of the gardens is the primary transport between the crown of Teldrassil and its base. Stepping through it instantly transports travelers to Rut'theran Village, where ships and hippogryphs connect the night elves to darkshore and the wider world.",["al"]={"tree portal darnassus","pink tree portal","teleporter darnassus"},["q"]="What is the glowing pink portal in the gardens?"},{["a"]="The city's main bank is situated right in the Temple Gardens, housed in an open elven pavilion on the district's largest central island.",["al"]={"darnassus bank location","where is bank","banker darnassus"},["q"]="Where is the Darnassus bank located?"},{["a"]="The district takes its name from the magnificent Temple of the Moon, which sits directly adjacent to the gardens along their southern border.",["al"]={"temple gardens name origin","why temple gardens"},["q"]="Why are they called the Temple Gardens?"},{["a"]="Bridges branch out across the water from the gardens to nearly every quarter: the Cenarion Enclave to the north, the Craftsmen's, Warrior's, and Tradesmen's Terraces to the east, and the Temple of the Moon to the south.",["al"]={"where do temple gardens lead","bridges from temple gardens"},["q"]="Which districts connect to the Temple Gardens?"}},["kw"]={"bank","darnassus","portal","rut'theran","teldrassil","temple gardens","temple of the moon"},["n"]="Temple Gardens",["s"]="The Temple Gardens form the tranquil, water-filled heart of Darnassus, surrounding small islets just north of the Temple of the Moon. Decorated with bridges and pristine flora, the district hosts the city bank and the mystical tree portal leading to the base of Teldrassil.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning the waters at the center of Darnassus, the Temple Gardens serve as the crossroads of the night elven capital. Wooden bridges connect its landscaped islets to the Cenarion Enclave in the north, the bustling terraces to the east, and the grand sanctuary of the Temple of the Moon to the south. The night elves carefully shape the district's flowing waters and lush foliage, creating a serene atmosphere that offers rest to travelers and priestesses alike.",["t"]="Heart of the Elven Capital"},{["b"]="Beyond housing the city's central vault and bank on its main island, the Temple Gardens hold critical importance for travelers entering or leaving the World Tree. On the western bank of the gardens stands a massive, glowing pink tree portal. This magical archway provides instantaneous passage down through the boughs to Rut'theran Village at Teldrassil's base, connecting the isolated boughs to the coastal docks and flight paths.",["t"]="Gateway to Teldrassil"}}}}}
t["subzone:temple-of-the-moon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,378,29.664.0,24.544.0,33.245.0,39.261.0,45.247.0,36.220.0",["h"]="4b9516",["n"]="Templo de la Luna",["s"]="Templo de la Luna. El templo de la Luna se alza en Darnassus como el corazón espiritual del pueblo de los elfos de la noche y la sede del gobierno en Teldrassil. Presidido por la suma sacerdotisa Tyrande Susurravientos, el santuario sirve como cuartel general de las Hermanas de Elune. Sus imponentes niveles de mármol albergan una poza de la luna sagrada cuyas aguas benditas otorgan sanación y comunión con la Diosa de la Luna. Erigido poco después de la Tercera Guerra, cuando los elfos de la noche se asentaron en Teldrassil, el Templo de la Luna se cuenta entre las mayores estructuras de piedra construidas por manos kaldorei modernas. Gran parte de su mármol se extrajo del continente de Kalimdor y se transportó a través del mar mediante artes mágicas. En el centro de su interior yace una amplia poza de la luna custodiada por la estatua de Haidene, donde aguas consagradas irradian un poder sereno. Más allá de servir como lugar de culto y reflexión apacible para los peregrinos, el templo funciona como la cúspide política de Darnassus, albergando a la suma sacerdotisa Tyrande Susurravientos mientras guía a su pueblo en los albores de una nueva y convulsa era.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="For Alliance priests—especially night elves—the temple represents the supreme font of Elune's divine mandate and the home of their highest trainers.",["race:NightElf"]="The temple stands as the cultural, spiritual, and civic core of modern kaldorei life, uniting the Sisterhood of Elune and the governance of Teldrassil under one roof."},["faq"]={{["a"]="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind presides over the temple. As the leader of the Sisterhood of Elune and de facto head of the kaldorei government, she holds court on the upper tiers, guiding both the spiritual and military affairs of Darnassus.",["al"]={"temple of the moon leader","who is in the temple","tyrande location"},["q"]="Who leads the Temple of the Moon?"},{["a"]="While Teldrassil was grown from boughs across the ocean, the temple itself is one of the few large stone edifices in Darnassus. Its marble and masonry were quarried from the mainland of Kalimdor and moved to the world tree's summit using magical transportation.",["al"]={"how was temple of the moon built","stone temple darnassus origins"},["q"]="How was the temple built on Teldrassil?"},{["a"]="The central pool is a sacred moonwell watched over by the statue of Haidene. Its waters are deeply consecrated and revered as the direct blessing of Elune, utilized by the Sisterhood for cleansing rites, meditation, and powerful restorative magic.",["al"]={"temple moonwell","water in temple of the moon"},["q"]="What is the pool in the center of the temple?"},{["a"]="The temple acts as the primary hub for Priest training in Darnassus. Adventurers also arrive here to report to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and receive guidance or assignments dispatched by the Sisterhood of Elune.",["al"]={"what is in temple of elune","temple trainers darnassus"},["q"]="What services can players find here?"}},["kw"]={"darnassus","haidene","moonwell","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil","temple of elune","temple of the moon","tyrande whisperwind"},["n"]="Temple of the Moon",["s"]="The Temple of the Moon stands in Darnassus as the spiritual heart of the night elven people and the seat of government on Teldrassil. Presided over by High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, the sanctuary serves as the headquarters for the Sisterhood of Elune. Its towering marble tiers house a sacred moonwell whose blessed waters bring healing and communion with the Moon Goddess.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Erected shortly after the Third War when the night elves settled Teldrassil, the Temple of the Moon is among the largest stone structures constructed by modern kaldorei hands. Much of its marble was quarried from the Kalimdor mainland and transported across the sea through magical means. At the center of its interior lies an expansive moonwell overseen by the statue of Haidene, where consecrated waters radiate quiet power. Beyond serving as a place of worship and quiet reflection for pilgrims, the temple functions as the political apex of Darnassus, housing High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind as she guides her people through the dawn of a uncertain new age.",["t"]="Sanctuary of the Moon Goddess"},{["b"]="Within the temple's quiet terraces, the priestesses of the Sisterhood of Elune carry out the goddess's will both spiritually and tactically. From here, emissaries and dispatched sisters are sent outward across northern Kalimdor to investigate threats or offer aid to local sentinels, such as Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde's inquiries along the Darkshore coastline. Novices and veteran priestesses alike gather beneath the starry vaulted ceiling to train in divine spellwork, tend to the wounded, and guard the sanctum from outside corruption.",["t"]="The Sisterhood's Bastion"}}}}}
t["subzone:the-den"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,253,19.447.0,18.241.0,31.278.0,31.254.0,39.223.0",["h"]="3d91ad",["n"]="El Cubil",["s"]="El Cubil. El Cubil es la cueva protegida situada en el corazón del Valle de los Retos, en el suroeste de Durotar. Al servir como base principal de operaciones para los jóvenes aventureros orcos y trols, les proporciona entrenamiento marcial y mágico antes de que se adentren en el resto del mundo. Ubicado en las paredes de los cañones rojos del Valle de los Retos, El Cubil sirve como un austero campo de pruebas. Dentro de su sombrío interior excavado, los luchadores novatos, lanzadores de conjuros y cazadores se presentan ante veteranos como Gornek y Vistalonga. Es aquí donde los recién llegados reciben su instrucción de combate básica, suministros y sus primeros ritos de iniciación, templándolos para las duras realidades de Durotar y los mayores desafíos que afronta la nueva Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Orc"]="Every young orc begins their journey at the Den, shedding the complacency of internment camps and blood haze to earn their place through discipline and labor.",["race:Troll"]="Following the devastation of the Darkspear Isles, young Darkspear trolls train in the Den alongside their orc allies, proving their mettle under the Horde's banner."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Den serves as the central command post and training sanctuary within the Valley of Trials. Here, novice orcs and Darkspear trolls gather to learn basic class techniques, purchase provisions, and receive assignments that prove their loyalty and combat readiness to the Horde.",["al"]={"what is the den","why is the den here","purpose of the den"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Den?"},{["a"]="The encampment is supervised by veteran overseers such as Gornek and Foreman Thazz'ril, along with spiritual and magical mentors like Zureetha Fargaze and Canaga Earthcaller, all working together to instruct the newest generation of warriors and mystics.",["al"]={"who leads the den","who is in charge","den overseer"},["q"]="Who runs things inside the Den?"},{["a"]="No. The Den only hosts basic class trainers and general equipment merchants. New adventurers must travel north to Razor Hill or on to Orgrimmar to study primary trade skills such as Blacksmithing, Leatherworking, or Mining.",["al"]={"profession trainers den","can i learn blacksmithing here","train mining in den"},["q"]="Can you learn primary professions here?"}},["kw"]={"durotar","gornek","starting cave","the den","trainers","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},["n"]="The Den",["s"]="The Den is the sheltered cave at the heart of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar. Serving as the primary base of operations for young orc and troll adventurers, it provides martial and magical training before they set out into the wider world.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked into the red canyon walls of the Valley of Trials, the Den serves as an austere proving ground. Within its carved, shadowy interior, novice fighters, spellcasters, and hunters report to veterans like Gornek and Zureetha Fargaze. It is here that fledglings receive their foundational combat instruction, supplies, and initial rites of passage, hardening them for the harsh realities of Durotar and the greater struggles facing the new Horde.",["t"]="Cradle of the Horde"},{["b"]="Beyond housing class trainers and provisions, the Den functions as an active field redoubt. Between dispatching new recruits to cull the local beasts and aggressive quillboars, the overseers maintain a strict, vigilant watch over the valley.",["t"]="A Watchful Outpost"}}}}}
t["subzone:the-loch"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,227,19.414.0,24.373.0,17.221.0,28.225.0,31.194.0,46.181.0",["h"]="8c338f",["n"]="Loch Modan",["s"]="Loch Modan. Loch Modan es el vasto lago de agua dulce que domina el valle de Loch Modan. Contenido por la monumental Presa de las Tres Cabezas, es la mayor masa de agua de Khaz Modan y el sustento vital de los asentamientos enanos de los alrededores. Loch Modan, que se extiende por el centro de la región de Loch Modan, se encuentra entre los lagos interiores más grandes del mundo conocido, rivalizando únicamente con el Lago Lordamere y el Lago Darrowmere en el norte. Sus aguas sustentan a los pescadores locales y proporcionan un plácido telón de fondo para la localidad de Thelsamar y los pabellones de caza cercanos. Sin embargo, bajo su calma superficie merodean agresivos treseladones y bestias de agua dulce que hacen de cruzarlo a nado una peligrosa empresa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The tranquil waters of The Loch provide vital freshwater and trade routes between Ironforge's central valley and the surrounding outposts.",["race:Dwarf"]="The Loch is a centerpiece of Ironforge pride, demonstrating how dwarven masonry and the Stonewrought Dam can tame nature to sustain settlements like Thelsamar."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Loch is the massive mountain lake that fills the center of the Loch Modan valley in Khaz Modan. It is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the world and defines the geography and livelihood of the local dwarves.",["al"]={"the loch lore","what is the loch lake","loch modan lake"},["q"]="What is The Loch?"},{["a"]="The lake is contained to the north by the Stonewrought Dam, a towering dwarven construction. The dam holds back countless gallons of water that would otherwise spill down through the mountain pass into the low-lying Wetlands.",["al"]={"why doesn't the loch drain","what holds the loch back","stonewrought dam purpose"},["q"]="How does the lake stay full?"},{["a"]="Not entirely. While local fishermen dot the shores and piers, deeper waters are home to predatory threshadons and snapping beasts that frequently attack unwary travelers venturing far from land.",["al"]={"loch monsters","swimming the loch","creatures in the loch"},["q"]="Is it safe to swim in The Loch?"},{["a"]="It is the largest body of water on the continent of Khaz Modan and the third largest known lake in the Eastern Kingdoms, behind only Lordamere Lake and Darrowmere Lake in Lordaeron.",["al"]={"biggest lake","the loch size comparison","how big is the loch"},["q"]="How large is The Loch compared to other lakes?"}},["kw"]={"khaz modan","lake","loch modan","stonewrought dam","the loch","thelsamar","threshadon","wetlands"},["n"]="The Loch",["s"]="The Loch is the vast freshwater lake that dominates the valley of Loch Modan. Held back by the monumental Stonewrought Dam, it is the largest body of water on Khaz Modan and the lifeblood of the surrounding dwarven settlements.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning the center of Loch Modan, The Loch is among the largest inland lakes in the known world, rivaled only by Lordamere Lake and Darrowmere Lake in the north. Its waters support local fishermen and provide a peaceful backdrop for the town of Thelsamar and nearby hunting lodges. Beneath its calm surface, however, prowl aggressive threshadons and freshwater beasts that make swimming across a perilous venture.",["t"]="Heart of the Valley"},{["b"]="The Loch exists in its current tranquil state thanks to masterwork dwarven engineering. To the north stands the massive Stonewrought Dam, an architectural marvel built across the mountain cleft to prevent the lake from flooding out into the Wetlands below. Maintaining this colossal structure is essential to preserving the valley's ecosystem and keeping Khaz Modan secure.",["t"]="The Stonewrought Barrier"}}}}}
t["subzone:thistlefur-hold"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,256,15.531.0,24.193.0,48.200.0,31.160.0,47.153.0",["h"]="f337a3",["n"]="Bastión Piel de Cardo",["s"]="Bastión Piel de Cardo. Bastión Piel de Cardo es una guarida cavernosa excavada al norte del Poblado Piel de Cardo, en la zona centro-oeste de Vallefresno. Antaño osos pacíficos del bosque, los fúrbolgs Piel de Cardo que residen aquí han sucumbido a la corrupción y se vuelven violentos contra cualquier forastero que se acerque. Ubicado en los confines septentrionales del Poblado Piel de Cardo, Bastión Piel de Cardo sirve como el corazón del territorio de la tribu Piel de Cardo. Los fúrbolgs de este lugar enloquecieron tras entrar en posesión del Ídolo de Remulos, cayendo en un estado de hostilidad salvaje que los hace peligrosos tanto para los viajeros como para sus vecinos. En lo profundo de las serpenteantes cavernas, la tribu acumula reliquias saqueadas —incluidos unos talismanes trol de interés para los Lanza Negra— y retiene a cautivos atados en jaulas de madera, como el aprisionado valiente tauren Ruul Nevopezuña.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Seeing the Thistlefur furbolgs fall to madness under the sway of the Idol of Remulos is a tragic reminder of how easily nature's guardians can be corrupted in Ashenvale.",["faction:Horde"]="The hold represents both a rescue mission and a salvage operation for the Horde, demanding warriors enter the den to liberate Ruul Snowhoof and retrieve stolen troll charms."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thistlefur Hold is the subterranean cavern complex at the northern end of Thistlefur Village in west-central Ashenvale. It houses the densest population of the hostile Thistlefur furbolg tribe.",["al"]={"thistlefur hold info","what is this cave","thistlefur cave"},["q"]="What is Thistlefur Hold?"},{["a"]="The Thistlefur furbolgs were corrupted by the Idol of Remulos, an artifact they kept within their possession. The malign influence twisted their minds and drove them to lash out against all outsiders.",["al"]={"why are thistlefur mad","thistlefur corruption","why are furbolgs attacking"},["q"]="Why are the furbolgs in Thistlefur Hold hostile?"},{["a"]="Ruul Snowhoof, a tauren brave, was captured by the Thistlefur tribe and sits locked in a wooden cage deep inside the caverns awaiting rescue by Horde champions.",["al"]={"thistlefur captive","tauren in thistlefur hold","who is ruul snowhoof"},["q"]="Who is trapped inside the hold?"},{["a"]="The Horde seeks to free the captured tauren Ruul Snowhoof and recover valuable troll charms that the furbolgs have hoarded within the depths of the cave.",["al"]={"horde quests thistlefur","troll charms thistlefur"},["q"]="Why is the Horde interested in Thistlefur Hold?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","furbolg","remulos","ruul snowhoof","thistlefur hold","thistlefur village","troll charms"},["n"]="Thistlefur Hold",["s"]="Thistlefur Hold is a cavernous den carved into northern Thistlefur Village in west-central Ashenvale. Once peaceful bears of the forest, the Thistlefur furbolgs residing here have succumbed to corruption and turn violent toward any outsider who draws near.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked into the northern reaches of Thistlefur Village, Thistlefur Hold serves as the heart of the Thistlefur tribe's territory. The furbolgs here were driven mad after coming into possession of the Idol of Remulos, falling into a state of feral hostility that makes them dangerous to travelers and neighbors alike. Deep within the winding caverns, the tribe hordes scavenged relics—including troll charms of interest to the Darkspear—and keeps captives bound in wooden cages, such as the imprisoned tauren brave Ruul Snowhoof.",["t"]="A Corrupted Den"}}}}}
t["subzone:thistlefur-village"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,279,15.565.0,36.158.0,46.239.0,34.180.0,51.243.0",["h"]="6221f2",["n"]="Poblado Piel de Cardo",["s"]="Poblado Piel de Cardo. El Poblado Piel de Cardo es un extenso asentamiento escondido en el bosque al norte de Astranaar, en la zona centro-oeste de Vallefresno. Sirve como hogar principal de la tribu de fúrbolgs Piel de Cardo, quienes han caído presa de una oscura corrupción y asaltan con violencia a cualquier forastero que se acerque a sus guaridas. Situado justo al norte del refugio de los elfos de la noche de Astranaar, el Poblado Piel de Cardo formó parte en su día de las pacíficas comunidades boscosas nativas de Vallefresno. Sin embargo, la maligna corrupción que se ha filtrado en los antiguos bosques se ha apoderado por completo de la tribu Piel de Cardo. Ahora, totalmente enloquecidos y sumamente hostiles, los fúrbolgs vigilan con ferocidad los caminos que serpentean por su asentamiento. El clan responde ante dos caudillos excepcionalmente feroces, Dal Bloodclaw y Rorgish Jowl, cuya implacable agresión representa una amenaza constante para los viajeros y los asentamientos cercanos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The fallen state of the Thistlefur tribe serves as a grim reminder of the lingering taint afflicting the spirits and wildlife of Ashenvale, demanding vigilant cleansing from the Cenarion Circle.",["race:NightElf"]="For centuries, the night elves lived in harmony alongside the native furbolg tribes. Seeing the Thistlefur succumb to violent corruption so close to Astranaar is both a heartbreak and a dire security crisis for the Sentinels."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thistlefur Village is situated in the west-central reaches of Ashenvale, nestled deep in the woodland hills directly north of the night elf town of Astranaar.",["al"]={"thistlefur village location","where is thistlefur","thistlefur map"},["q"]="Where is Thistlefur Village located?"},{["a"]="The Thistlefur furbolgs have been gripped by the dark corruption spreading across the forests of Ashenvale. Driven mad by these foul influences, they view all outsiders as immediate enemies and attack anyone who approaches their territory.",["al"]={"why are thistlefur hostile","corrupted furbolgs thistlefur","why attack"},["q"]="Why are the furbolgs here attacking travelers?"},{["a"]="The tribe is led by two particularly fierce and brutal warrior chieftains named Dal Bloodclaw and Rorgish Jowl, who maintain vicious dominance over the village and its nearby dens.",["al"]={"thistlefur boss","thistlefur leaders","who leads thistlefur"},["q"]="Who leads the Thistlefur furbolgs?"},{["a"]="Yes. Because Thistlefur Village lies immediately north of Astranaar, the aggressive and unstable nature of the corrupted furbolgs makes them a persistent danger to night elf scouts, supply lines, and sentries stationed along the central roads.",["al"]={"thistlefur threat to astranaar","danger to astranaar"},["q"]="Does Thistlefur Village pose a danger to Astranaar?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","astranaar","corruption","dal bloodclaw","furbolg","rorgish jowl","thistlefur","village"},["n"]="Thistlefur Village",["s"]="Thistlefur Village is a sprawling settlement tucked into the forest north of Astranaar in west-central Ashenvale. It serves as the primary home of the Thistlefur furbolg tribe, who have fallen prey to dark corruption and violently assault any outsiders venturing near their dens.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated just north of the night elf haven of Astranaar, Thistlefur Village was once part of the peaceful woodland communities native to Ashenvale. However, the malignant corruption that has seeped into the ancient forests has entirely claimed the Thistlefur tribe. Now thoroughly maddened and intensely hostile, the furbolgs fiercely guard the paths winding through their settlement. The clan answers to two exceptionally ferocious chieftains, Dal Bloodclaw and Rorgish Jowl, whose unyielding aggression poses a constant threat to travelers and nearby settlements.",["t"]="A Corrupted Den"}}}}}
t["subzone:thistlefuzz-arcanery"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,374,28.565.0,38.185.0,46.231.0,63.264.0",["h"]="6a0b6a",["n"]="Taller Arcano Cardopelusa",["s"]="Taller Arcano Cardopelusa. Taller Arcano Cardopelusa es un destacado taller y academia de las artes mágicas situado al este de la Gran Fundición en Forjaz. Regentado principalmente por practicantes gnomos, sirve como el principal refugio de la capital para encantadores y eruditos que buscan imbuir magia en el metal y el pergamino. Sus concurridas estancias vibran con energía arcana justo al lado de los rugientes fuegos de la industria enana. Ubicado justo al este de la atronadora Gran Fundición, Taller Arcano Cardopelusa ofrece un marcado contraste con el resonar de los yunques de los herreros enanos. En sus dos niveles, eruditos, practicantes y aprendices se reúnen para dominar las sutiles disciplinas del encantamiento y el estudio mágico. Mientras que los enanos de Forjaz prefieren moldear el acero a fuerza de músculo y fuego, los gnomos del taller arcano demuestran cómo la energía arcana pura puede ligarse directamente a armas, armaduras y curiosas herramientas. Se erige como un santuario esencial para los lanzadores de conjuros que transitan por la fortaleza de la montaña.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Visiting mages find familiar reagents, quiet corners of theory, and kindred spellcasters among the otherwise martial, weapon-focused halls of the dwarf capital.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes residing in Ironforge, Thistlefuzz Arcanery is a comfortable reminder of their love for arcane theory, technical study, and delicate experimentation amidst a city dominated by heavy dwarven iron."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thistlefuzz Arcanery sits along the eastern ring of the Great Forge in central Ironforge, easily identified by the arcane apparatuses and enchanting supplies displayed around its doors.",["al"]={"arcanery location","where is thistlefuzz","ironforge enchanting shop"},["q"]="Where is Thistlefuzz Arcanery located?"},{["a"]="The shop caters to practitioners of magical crafts. Enchanting trainers, spellcraft suppliers, and scholars gather here to teach apprentices, trade rare reagents, and conduct experiments away from the physical soot of the smithies.",["al"]={"what is in thistlefuzz arcanery","trainers in thistlefuzz"},["q"]="What services are offered inside the Arcanery?"},{["a"]="Positioning an enchanting workshop right beside the Great Forge is practical. Newly forged blades, armor plates, and mechanical components produced by the dwarven smiths can immediately be carried east to be imbued with protective enchantments and elemental power.",["al"]={"why is it near the forge","arcanery great forge connection"},["q"]="Why is an arcane workshop situated so close to the Great Forge?"}},["kw"]={"arcane","enchanter","enchanting","gnome","great forge","ironforge","thistlefuzz arcanery"},["n"]="Thistlefuzz Arcanery",["s"]="Thistlefuzz Arcanery is a prominent workshop and academy of the magical arts located east of the Great Forge in Ironforge. Run primarily by gnome practitioners, it serves as the capital's premier haven for enchanters and scholars seeking to weave magic into metal and parchment. Its busy chambers hum with arcane energy right alongside the roaring fires of dwarven industry.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked directly east of the thundering Great Forge, Thistlefuzz Arcanery offers a stark contrast to the clanging anvils of dwarven smiths. Within its two levels, scholars, practitioners, and apprentices gather to master the subtle disciplines of enchanting and magical study. While the Ironforge dwarves prefer to reshape steel through muscle and fire, the gnomes of the Arcanery demonstrate how raw arcane energy can be bound directly into weaponry, armor, and curious tools. It stands as an essential sanctuary for spellcasters navigating the mountain stronghold.",["t"]="Arcane Craft in the Mountain"}}}}}
t["subzone:three-corners"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,386,28.513.0,39.182.0,38.217.0,45.216.0",["h"]="e703eb",["n"]="Tres Caminos",["s"]="Tres Caminos. Tres Caminos es una encrucijada vital situada justo en el interior de la frontera occidental de las Montañas Crestagrana. Al ramificarse hacia los tres pueblos vecinos de Villadorada, Villa del Lago y Villa Oscura, marca el límite entre el corazón del reino y las peligrosas tierras salvajes de Crestagrana. Una torre de vigilancia de la guardia de Ventormenta se alza sobre la intersección, manteniendo la línea contra las jaurías de gnolls que intentan avanzar. Situado en el extremo occidental de las Montañas Crestagrana, Tres Caminos conecta tres asentamientos clave de la Alianza: Villadorada en el Bosque de Elwynn al oeste, Villa del Lago al noreste y Villa Oscura en el Bosque del Ocaso al sur. Debido a esta unión estratégica, Ventormenta erigió Torre de Vigilancia en el centro de la encrucijada. Al custodiar el puesto, los guardias y exploradores locales intentan mantener las vías despejadas de los agresivos gnolls de Crestagrana, que amenazan constantemente a los viajeros y carromatos de suministros que transitan entre las regiones.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers leaving the relative safety of Elwynn Forest, Three Corners is the first fortified outpost and a stark reminder that Stormwind's grip on its borderlands is stretched thin.",["race:Human"]="The watchtower links the southern human heartlands, serving as a critical junction for couriers and trade moving between Elwynn, Duskwood, and Redridge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The crossroads splits into three distinct roads heading toward the 'Three Shires' of southern Stormwind: Goldshire in Elwynn Forest, Lakeshire in Redridge, and Darkshire in Duskwood.",["al"]={"three corners name meaning","why three corners","three corners history"},["q"]="Why is this place called Three Corners?"},{["a"]="The outpost, known as Tower Watch, is manned by members of the Stormwind Guard. They serve as an early warning post and defensive bulwark against gnolls venturing down from the Redridge peaks toward the Elwynn border.",["al"]={"who controls three corners","tower watch guards","who is in the tower"},["q"]="Who guards the tower at Three Corners?"},{["a"]="Gnolls from the surrounding hills constantly prowl the roadway, ambushing travelers and couriers. The guards stationed here regularly call upon passing adventurers to cull the gnoll packs and keep the roads passable.",["al"]={"three corners monsters","dangers at three corners","three corners gnolls"},["q"]="What threats are active around Three Corners?"}},["kw"]={"crossroads","darkshire","gnolls","goldshire","lakeshire","redridge","three corners","tower watch"},["n"]="Three Corners",["s"]="Three Corners is a vital crossroads nestled just inside the western border of the Redridge Mountains. Branching toward the three neighboring towns of Goldshire, Lakeshire, and Darkshire, it marks the boundary between the heart of the kingdom and Redridge's perilous wilderness. A Stormwind Guard watchtower stands over the intersection, holding the line against encroaching gnoll packs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated at the western edge of the Redridge Mountains, Three Corners connects three key Alliance settlements: Goldshire in Elwynn Forest to the west, Lakeshire to the northeast, and Darkshire in Duskwood to the south. Because of this strategic junction, Stormwind erected Tower Watch at the center of the crossroads. Manning the post, local guards and scouts attempt to keep the thoroughfares clear of Redridge's aggressive gnolls, who constantly threaten travelers and supply wagons passing between the regions.",["t"]="A Crossroads of Three Shires"}}}}}
t["subzone:thunder-falls"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,246,24.529.0,31.232.0,42.247.0,43.207.0",["h"]="adfa6f",["n"]="Cataratas del Trueno",["s"]="Cataratas del Trueno. Cataratas del Trueno es un barranco de montaña apartado, escondido en las alturas noroccidentales de Bosque de Elwynn. Protegido entre escarpados acantilados y alimentado por estruendosas cascadas, cuenta con una tranquila cabaña junto al río que ha caído en manos de bandidos locales. Escondidas en las escarpadas crestas sobre Lago Espejo, Cataratas del Trueno es una inusual hendidura geográfica. El barranco está excavado por un rápido arroyo de montaña que entra a través de una cascada inaccesible por el norte, para luego precipitarse a ambos lados en impresionantes saltos de agua. Uno de los lados cae directamente a Lago Espejo, mientras que el curso río abajo fluye hacia el oeste, en dirección a las agrestes fronteras de Páramos de Poniente. A pesar del rugido de las aguas, en la orilla se asientan una pequeña cabaña, un muelle y una forja al aire libre, aunque los forajidos ahora reclaman este apacible claro para sí mismos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={},["faq"]={{["a"]="You can reach Thunder Falls by heading to the northern side of Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest. A steep, narrow trail winds up into the hills along the right side of the Mirror Lake waterfall, leading directly into the secluded ravine.",["al"]={"how to get to thunder falls","thunder falls location","where is thunder falls"},["q"]="How do you reach Thunder Falls?"},{["a"]="The secluded cabin appears to have once belonged to a solitary fisherman or frontiersman, complete with a dock, rowing boat, and outdoor anvil. Today, however, it serves as a remote hideout for bandits operating in the wilderness of Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"who is at the cottage","thunder falls house","cottage bandits"},["q"]="Who lives in the cottage at Thunder Falls?"},{["a"]="The stream flows through the narrow mountain gap from an upper mountain cascade. Downstream, it winds past the cottage and cascades down another steep fall that empties near the eastern boundary of Westfall.",["al"]={"where does the water go","thunder falls river"},["q"]="Where does the river at Thunder Falls flow?"}},["kw"]={"bandits","cottage","elwynn forest","mirror lake","thunder falls","waterfall"},["n"]="Thunder Falls",["s"]="Thunder Falls is a secluded mountain ravine tucked away in the northwestern heights of Elwynn Forest. Cradled between sheer cliffs and fed by roaring cascades, it features a quiet riverside cottage that has fallen into the hands of local bandits.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the jagged ridges above Mirror Lake, Thunder Falls is an unusual geographical cleft. The ravine is carved by a swift mountain stream that enters via an inaccessible northern cascade, only to drop away on both sides in dramatic waterfalls. One side plunges down into Mirror Lake, while the downstream course flows west toward the rugged borders of Westfall. Despite the roaring waters, a small cottage, a dock, and an outdoor forge sit along the shore, though outlaws now claim the peaceful clearing for themselves.",["t"]="A Hidden Mountain Hollow"}}}}}
t["subzone:thunderhorn-water-well"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,373,20.585.0,44.142.0,47.252.0,28.210.1",["h"]="969bea",["n"]="Pozo Tronacuerno",["s"]="Pozo Tronacuerno. El Pozo Tronacuerno es una fuente de agua vital situada en las llanuras onduladas del centro de Mulgore, a lo largo del camino entre el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre y Cima del Trueno. Como todos los pozos del valle, proporciona un sustento esencial a las tribus y a las manadas que recorren los pastizales. Mantener esta agua limpia y protegida es crucial para preservar la vida en la tierra natal de los tauren. Situado en medio de los extensos pastizales del centro de Mulgore, el Pozo Tronacuerno se nutre directamente de los acuíferos puros que alimentan el valle. Para los tauren nómadas y sus aldeas recién asentadas, estos pozos comunales representan la vida, el sustento y la generosidad de la Madre Tierra. Dado que el agua es un bien preciado en las llanuras bañadas por el sol, controlar los pozos significa controlar la tierra misma. Intrusos como Ventura y Cía. han puesto sus ojos en estas fuentes en repetidas ocasiones, intentando aprovecharlas para la explotación industrial y alterando el frágil equilibrio que las tribus luchan por preservar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Shaman deeply revere the pure water springs of Mulgore, viewing the protection of water spirits and subterranean currents as a sacred duty.",["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, wells like Thunderhorn are vital lifelines gifted by the Earth Mother, requiring constant guardianship against foreign polluters and greedy trespassers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The well is located in central Mulgore, situated along the north-south road running between Bloodhoof Village and the bluffs of Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"thunderhorn well location","where is thunderhorn well","thunderhorn water well map"},["q"]="Where is the Thunderhorn Water Well located?"},{["a"]="The water wells of Mulgore tap into the pristine subterranean waters of the valley, sustaining the herds, pilgrims, and settlements. To the tauren, water is a sacred gift from the Earth Mother that must be safeguarded from outside corruption and greed.",["al"]={"why is thunderhorn well important","tauren water wells meaning","why protect the wells"},["q"]="Why is this water well important to the tauren?"},{["a"]="Goblins of the Venture Company attempted to seize control of the well to monopolize the valley's water supply for their nearby mining and logging ventures, but local tauren fought back to reclaim and purify it.",["al"]={"who attacked the well","venture co well","enemies at thunderhorn well"},["q"]="Who has threatened the well?"}},["kw"]={"bloodhoof","mulgore","thunder bluff","thunderhorn","venture company","water","well"},["n"]="Thunderhorn Water Well",["s"]="Thunderhorn Water Well is a vital water source situated in the rolling plains of central Mulgore along the path between Bloodhoof Village and Thunder Bluff. Like all the wells across the valley, it provides essential nourishment to the tribes and the herds roaming the grasslands. Keeping this water clean and defended is crucial to maintaining life in the tauren homeland.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated amid the sprawling grasslands of central Mulgore, the Thunderhorn Water Well taps directly into the pure aquifers feeding the valley. For the nomadic tauren and their newly settled villages, these communal wells represent life, sustenance, and the Earth Mother's bounty. Because water is precious across the sun-drenched plains, controlling the wells means controlling the land itself. Intruders such as the Venture Company have repeatedly eyed these sources, attempting to harness them for industrial exploitation and disrupt the fragile balance the tribes fight to preserve.",["t"]="A Life-Giving Spring"}}}}}
t["subzone:tidus-stair"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,254,16.579.0,29.153.0,25.174.0,42.242.0,49.135.0",["h"]="c8c5e8",["n"]="El Escalón de la Marea",["s"]="El Escalón de la Marea. El Escalón de la Marea es una formación rocosa natural de amplias terrazas escalonadas de piedra situadas sobre La Costa Mercante, al sureste de Trinquete. Al abrigo del Mare Magnum, sirve como un apacible retiro para dos chamanes tauren que comulgan con las mareas y los espíritus del agua. Al descender hacia el oleaje al sureste de Trinquete, El Escalón de la Marea parece un conjunto monumental de escalones de piedra desgastada tallados directamente en los acantilados costeros. Aunque Los Baldíos circundantes son áridos, polvorientos y propensos a escaramuzas, este tramo tranquilo con vistas a La Costa Mercante está dominado por el sonido del romper de las olas. En lo alto de las terrazas se encuentra una modesta choza donde residen los tauren Islen Vident'aqua y Mahren Visioceleste. Lejos de los bulliciosos muelles comerciales de los goblins, ambos pasan sus días pescando, contemplando el horizonte y buscando el conocimiento de los espíritus del agua de la costa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Every Horde shaman eventually journeys down these coastal steps to seek out Islen Waterseer during their trials to bind the water totem.",["race:Tauren"]="The quiet presence of Islen Waterseer and Mahren Skyseer shows how tauren seers maintain a spiritual vigil even far outside Mulgore's borders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tidus Stair lies along the eastern coast of the Barrens, directly southeast of the goblin port of Ratchet. It overlooks the waters of the Merchant Coast.",["al"]={"tidus stair location","where is tidus stair","how to get to tidus stair"},["q"]="Where is Tidus Stair located?"},{["a"]="Two tauren make their home here: Islen Waterseer and Mahren Skyseer. They live in a simple seaside hut on the terraces, spending their time fishing and communing with nature.",["al"]={"who is at tidus stair","tidus stair npcs","who lives here"},["q"]="Who lives at Tidus Stair?"},{["a"]="Horde shamans seeking to master the element of water are guided across Kalimdor to find Islen Waterseer at Tidus Stair. Here, beside the open ocean, initiates learn to commune with the tides and seek out pure waters to bind their water totem.",["al"]={"shaman tidus stair","water totem tidus stair","why do shamans come here"},["q"]="Why is Tidus Stair significant to shamans?"},{["a"]="The resident tauren are loyal to the Horde and guide Horde shamans, though the remote terraces sit outside any formal military borders.",["al"]={"is tidus stair horde","tidus stair faction"},["q"]="Is Tidus Stair aligned with the Horde or neutral?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","islen waterseer","mahren skyseer","merchant coast","ratchet","tidus stair","water totem"},["n"]="Tidus Stair",["s"]="Tidus Stair is a natural rock formation of broad, stepped stone terraces perched over the Merchant Coast southeast of Ratchet. Sheltered beside the Great Sea, it serves as a quiet retreat for two tauren shamans communing with the tides and water spirits.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Descending toward the surf southeast of Ratchet, the Tidus Stair resembles a monumental set of weathered stone steps cut directly into the coastal bluffs. While the surrounding Barrens are arid, dusty, and prone to skirmishes, this quiet stretch overlooking the Merchant Coast is dominated by the sound of crashing waves. Perched on the terraces is a modest hut where the tauren Islen Waterseer and Mahren Skyseer reside. Far from the bustling trade docks of the goblins, the two spend their days fishing, watching the horizon, and seeking insight from the coastal water spirits.",["t"]="Steps to the Sea"}}}}}
t["subzone:tinkers-court"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,205,27.487.0,24.470.1,48.292.0,32.176.0,45.157.0,61.209.0",["h"]="0b210b",["n"]="Cámara de los Manitas",["s"]="Cámara de los Manitas. Cámara de los Manitas es la gran cámara del consejo situada en el corazón de Gnomeregan. Antaño la bulliciosa sede del Manitas Mayor y su consejo de gobierno, en la actualidad es el lúgubre bastión del traidor Mekigeniero Termochufe. Antes del desastre que asoló Gnomeregan, Cámara de los Manitas servía como el corazón cívico y político de la nación. Era aquí donde el Manitas Mayor Gelbin Mekkatorque se reunía con consejeros y maestros inventores, incluido el Maestro manitas Sobrechispa, para debatir sobre avances tecnológicos, gobernar asuntos cívicos y guiar a la sociedad gnómica. La corte representaba la cúspide del ingenio y el gobierno de los gnomos, situada justo más allá de las obras industriales de Laboratorios de Ingeniería y Hangar de Lanzamiento.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="The chamber is an alarming showcase of corrupted engineering, filled with deadly bomb delivery systems and the lethal siege suit operated by Thermaplugg.",["race:Gnome"]="Standing in the Tinkers' Court is a painful reminder of betrayal; this room was once where gnomish leaders gathered before Sicco Thermaplugg seized it amidst irradiated ruin."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Historically, the Tinkers' Court served as the meeting place and civic chamber for the elected High Tinker and the ruling council of Gnomeregan. Gelbin Mekkatorque and high-ranking advisors, such as Tinkmaster Overspark, used this hall to discuss city governance and cutting-edge innovations.",["al"]={"tinkers court history","what is tinkers court","original purpose of court"},["q"]="What was the Tinkers' Court used for originally?"},{["a"]="Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg currently occupies the court. Calling himself the King of Gnomeregan, he holds the chamber alongside his defensive machinery and irradiated minions.",["al"]={"who is in tinkers court","boss in tinkers court","thermaplugg room"},["q"]="Who controls Tinkers' Court now?"},{["a"]="Tinkers' Court lies in the deepest reaches of Gnomeregan, beyond the dark tunnels and lower levels connected to both the Launch Bay and the Engineering Labs.",["al"]={"where is tinkers court","how to get to tinkers court","find tinkers court"},["q"]="Where is the court located within Gnomeregan?"},{["a"]="Reaching the court is the ultimate objective of reclaiming the city, as Mekgineer Thermaplugg directs his irradiated minions from within. Deposing him is the critical first step toward Gnomeregan's liberation.",["al"]={"why go to tinkers court","kill thermaplugg why","importance of tinkers court"},["q"]="Why is reaching Tinkers' Court so important for the Alliance?"}},["kw"]={"council","gnomeregan","high tinker","mekkatorque","overspark","thermaplugg","tinkers court"},["n"]="Tinkers' Court",["s"]="Tinkers' Court is the grand council chamber at the heart of Gnomeregan. Once the bustling seat of the High Tinker and his ruling council, it is now the grim stronghold of the traitor Mekgineer Thermaplugg.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the disaster that ruined Gnomeregan, the Tinkers' Court served as the civic and political heart of the nation. It was here that High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque gathered with advisors and master inventors, including Tinkmaster Overspark, to debate technological advancements, govern civic matters, and guide gnomish society. The court represented the pinnacle of gnomish ingenuity and governance, situated just beyond the industrial works of the Engineering Labs and the Launch Bay.",["t"]="Seat of the Gnomish Council"},{["b"]="Following the disastrous radiation venting that drove the gnomes into exile, Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg claimed the chamber as his own. Styling himself the King of Gnomeregan, the mad inventor now sits in the Tinkers' Court surrounded by twisted contraptions, loyal leper gnomes, and bomb dispensers. From this desecrated council hall, he directs his remaining forces, making the court the final and most dangerous threshold for any strike team seeking to end his rule.",["t"]="Thermaplugg's Throneroom"}}}}}
t["subzone:tiragarde-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,360,20.550.0,26.519.0,32.220.0,53.232.0,28.177.0,43.324.0",["h"]="50d6ba",["n"]="Fuerte de Tiragarde",["s"]="Fuerte de Tiragarde. El Fuerte de Tiragarde es un bastión humano fortificado situado en la Costa de la Huída de Durotar, al sur de Cerrotajo. Construida originalmente durante la invasión del Gran Almirante Daelin Valiente, la ciudadela en ruinas sigue contando con una guarnición de infantes de marina hostiles de Kul Tiras a las órdenes del Lieutenant Benedict. Representa una desafiante espina clavada en el costado de la Horda, justo en su propio territorio. Erigido durante la campaña del Gran Almirante Daelin Valiente para erradicar el recién fundado reino de Thrall, el Fuerte de Tiragarde proporcionó a la flota de Kul Tiras una cabeza de playa atrincherada en las costas rojas de Durotar. Aunque la Horda acabó rompiendo el asedio y mató a Valiente en la Isla Theramore, el fuerte nunca se abandonó del todo. Las fuerzas de reabastecimiento bajo el mando del Lieutenant Benedict recuperaron los muros de piedra derruidos, siguiendo las órdenes permanentes del difunto almirante de librar una guerra implacable contra los orcos y rechazando por completo la paz forjada por Lady Jaina Valiente.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Tiragarde Keep is a blatant Alliance invasion base right on Durotar's doorstep; raiding its ramparts and eliminating Lieutenant Benedict is a rite of passage for young soldiers serving Razor Hill.",["race:Human"]="The garrison represents the unbending, vengeful legacy of Kul Tiras and Admiral Proudmoore, fighting a stubborn guerrilla war in defiance of Jaina Proudmoore's diplomacy."},["faq"]={{["a"]="These humans are Kul Tiras sailors and marines who arrived with Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore during his invasion following the Third War. They reject peace with the Horde and maintain this garrison to harass the orcs.",["al"]={"why are alliance here","who are the humans in tiragarde","human soldiers durotar"},["q"]="Why are there humans in Durotar?"},{["a"]="No. While Jaina Proudmoore rules Theramore Isle and maintains an uneasy truce with Thrall, these soldiers follow the orders of her late father, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. They consider any peace with orcs unacceptable treason.",["al"]={"is tiragarde theramore","are they jaina proudmoore's men","theramore soldiers here"},["q"]="Are these humans part of Jaina's forces in Theramore?"},{["a"]="The stronghold is commanded by Lieutenant Benedict, a Kul Tiran officer acting on posthumous invasion orders left by Admiral Proudmoore to secure the coast and attack the Horde.",["al"]={"tiragarde boss","who leads tiragarde keep","lieutenant benedict"},["q"]="Who commands Tiragarde Keep?"},{["a"]="The keep is fortified and manned by disciplined, well-armed Kul Tiran troops. While the defenders from Razor Hill frequently skirmish with the garrison and use it as a proving ground for new recruits, launching a full-scale siege would draw heavy casualties and divert vital resources away from securing the rest of Durotar.",["al"]={"why not destroy tiragarde","why is the keep still here"},["q"]="Why hasn't the Horde simply wiped them out?"}},["kw"]={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","razor hill","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep"},["n"]="Tiragarde Keep",["s"]="Tiragarde Keep is a fortified human stronghold situated along Durotar's Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill. Originally built during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion, the ruined citadel remains garrisoned by hostile Kul Tiran marines under Lieutenant Benedict. It serves as a defiant, permanent thorn in the Horde's side right on their home territory.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Erected during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's campaign to eradicate Thrall's newly founded realm, Tiragarde Keep provided the Kul Tiran fleet an entrenched beachhead on the red shores of Durotar. Although the Horde eventually broke the siege and killed Proudmoore at Theramore Isle, the keep was never fully abandoned. Resupply forces under Lieutenant Benedict reclaimed the shattered stone walls, following the late Admiral's standing orders to wage an unyielding war against the orcs, entirely refusing the peace forged by Lady Jaina Proudmoore.",["t"]="Proudmoore's Bastion"},{["b"]="Today, the keep's gleaming white battlements stand in harsh contrast against Durotar's crimson cliffs. Well-trained Kul Tiras sailors and marines patrol the ramparts and launch raids targeting supply lines near Razor Hill. For the Horde, Tiragarde Keep is an ongoing security crisis and a live proving ground. Orc and troll commanders constantly task young warriors with assaulting the fortress and cutting down Benedict's soldiers, seeking to contain the garrison before the humans can mount a deeper inland offensive.",["t"]="A Thorn in Durotar's Flank"}}}}}
t["subzone:tower-of-althalaxx"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,265,19.473.0,15.397.1,31.141.0,44.189.0,45.131.0,47.156.0",["h"]="435717",["n"]="Torre de Althalaxx",["s"]="Torre de Althalaxx. La Torre de Althalaxx es una antigua aguja de los Altonato situada en el norte de Costa Oscura, cerca de la costa. En su día fue un retiro aislado para el hechicero Athrikus Narassin antes del Gran Cataclismo, pero ahora se ha visto infestada de cultistas demoníacos y brujos que practican artes oscuras. Hace diez mil años, la Reina Azshara asentó a sirvientes Altonato predilectos en las poblaciones costeras de Ameth'Aran y Bashal'Aran, otorgando autoridad sobre ellos al poderoso hechicero Athrikus Narassin. Distanciándose del gobierno civil, Athrikus prefirió aislarse en la cercana Torre de Althalaxx. Cuando el Gran Cataclismo destrozó el antiguo Kalimdor, la torre resistió junto a la desolada costa de Costa Oscura, alzándose como una silenciosa ruina de magias élficas olvidadas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The dark rites conducted by the Cult of the Dark Strand demonstrate the far-reaching influence and lingering presence of the Shadow Council in Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="The tower represents a grim reminder of Highborne corruption and demonic folly lingering on ancestral lands, demanding swift intervention from Darnassus."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is an ancient elven mage tower built in northern Darkshore during the reign of Queen Azshara, now occupied by dark sorcerers and cultists.",["al"]={"tower of althalaxx","althalaxx tower","what is althalaxx"},["q"]="What is the Tower of Althalaxx?"},{["a"]="Athrikus Narassin, a powerful Highborne sorcerer appointed by Queen Azshara to oversee the nearby settlements of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, retreated here when he grew bored of his duties.",["al"]={"who lived here","athrikus narassin","who built the tower"},["q"]="Who originally built and lived in the tower?"},{["a"]="They belong to the Cult of the Dark Strand, a sect of warlocks, cultists, and satyrs practicing dark rites within the ruined tower.",["al"]={"who are the cultists","cult of the dark strand","althalaxx enemies"},["q"]="Who are the cultists occupying the tower now?"},{["a"]="The cultists conduct dark rituals and soul-binding magic, subjecting the long-dead elven spirits of ancient Darkshore to agonizing torment for their spells.",["al"]={"why are there ghosts","tortured spirits althalaxx"},["q"]="Why are there ghosts and tortured spirits here?"}},["kw"]={"althalaxx","ameth'aran","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","dark strand","darkshore","highborne","satyr","shadow council"},["n"]="Tower of Althalaxx",["s"]="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient Highborne spire standing in northern Darkshore near the coast. Once an isolated retreat for the sorcerer Athrikus Narassin before the Great Sundering, it has become infested by demonic cultists and warlocks practicing dark arts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne servants in the coastal towns of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, placing the powerful sorcerer Athrikus Narassin in authority over them. Growing distant from civic governance, Athrikus chose to isolate himself within the nearby Tower of Althalaxx. When the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, the tower endured along the desolate coastline of Darkshore, standing as a quiet ruin of forgotten elven magics.",["t"]="A Highborne Retreat"},{["b"]="In the modern era, the tower has stirred with malignant sorcery. Warlocks, dark cultists calling themselves the Cult of the Dark Strand, and allied satyrs have congregated within the ruin under the leadership of Athrikus Narassin himself. Their rites channel demonic magic and torment the lingering spirits of the ancient dead, serving sinister designs tied directly to the demonic Shadow Council.",["t"]="The Dark Strand"}}}}}
t["subzone:tower-of-azora"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,299,27.497.0,21.444.1,29.185.0,34.181.0,34.218.0,42.200.0",["h"]="19fae8",["n"]="Torre de Azora",["s"]="Torre de Azora. La Torre de Azora es una esbelta aguja de mago que se alza en la parte oriental del Bosque de Elwynn, al norte de la Plantación de Calabazas de Brackwell. Presidido por el archimago humano Theocritus, este enclave sirve como puesto académico inmerso en una silenciosa disputa mágica contra una torre hostil en las vecinas Montañas Crestagrana. Erigida junto al camino oriental hacia las Montañas Crestagrana, la Torre de Azora es un santuario arcano atendido casi en su totalidad por taumaturgos gnomos. Bajo la tutela del archimago Theocritus, estos eruditos estudian extrañas curiosidades y ofrecen instrucción mágica a los tejedores de hechizos errantes. El aura mágica salvaje que rodea la aguja altera en ocasiones a la fauna cercana, obligando a los sirvientes gnomos a lidiar con objetos domésticos encantados e insectos mutados que se cuelan por la entrada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="For mages traveling beyond Stormwind, the tower offers a secluded haven of study, arcane trainers, and a front-row seat to the dangerous arts of remote divination.",["race:Gnome"]="Seeing an arcane spire in human lands staffed by gnomes under Archmage Theocritus is a proud showcase of your people's mastery over the mystic arts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The tower is presided over by Archmage Theocritus, an accomplished human wizard. He directs the servants within the spire and coordinates their magical defenses against rival sorcerers.",["al"]={"who leads the tower of azora","who is in charge here","tower of azora boss"},["q"]="Who rules the Tower of Azora?"},{["a"]="The servants of Azora are predominantly gnome researchers and acolytes who assist Archmage Theocritus with his studies, arcane experiments, and housekeeping against magical mishaps.",["al"]={"why gnomes in elwynn tower","servants of azora"},["q"]="Why are there so many gnomes here?"},{["a"]="The tower is locked in a magical rivalry with the Tower of Ilgalar in the Redridge Mountains, home to the evil sorcerer Morganth. Both spires spy on each other with scrying artifacts and contest each other's influence.",["al"]={"azora enemy","tower feud","who is azora spying on"},["q"]="Who is the tower fighting against?"},{["a"]="The Eye of Azora is an enchanted scrying focus placed on a table in the upper sanctum. Touching it allows an observer to gaze through magical distance to monitor the outskirts of the Tower of Ilgalar.",["al"]={"orb on top floor","eye of azora","crystal ball azora"},["q"]="What is the Eye of Azora on the top floor?"}},["kw"]={"azora","elwynn","enchanting","ilgalar","morganth","scrying","spire","theocritus"},["n"]="Tower of Azora",["s"]="The Tower of Azora is a slender wizard's spire rising out of eastern Elwynn Forest, north of the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. Presided over by the human Archmage Theocritus, the enclave serves as a scholarly outpost locked in a silent magical feud with a hostile tower in neighboring Redridge Mountains.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing along the eastern road toward the Redridge Mountains, the Tower of Azora is an arcane sanctuary staffed almost entirely by gnome spellcasters. Under the stewardship of Archmage Theocritus, these scholars study strange curiosities and provide magical instruction to wandering spellweavers. The wild magical aura surrounding the spire occasionally warps the nearby wildlife, leaving the gnome servants to contend with enchanted household items and mutated insects creeping past the doorway.",["t"]="A Spire of Arcane Vigilance"},{["b"]="Beneath its quiet scholarly exterior, the tower is engaged in an enduring war of scrying and sabotage. To the east, atop the crags of Redridge, sits the sinister Tower of Ilgalar, ruled by the renegade sorcerer Morganth. Theocritus and Morganth constantly spy on one another through arcane means, employing daring adventurers to plant scrying relics like the Eye of Azora to pierce the wards of Ilgalar and monitor Morganth's dark machinations.",["t"]="The Feud with Ilgalar"}}}}}
t["subzone:trade-district"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,293,26.599.0,23.612.0,36.228.0,38.188.0,60.170.0,58.169.0",["h"]="f73013",["n"]="Distrito de Mercaderes",["s"]="Distrito de Mercaderes. El Distrito de Mercaderes es el bullicioso corazón comercial de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, situado justo después de las puertas principales y del Valle de los Héroes. Sirve como centro neurálgico tanto para aventureros como para ciudadanos, y alberga el banco central de la ciudad, la casa de subastas, el registro de hermandades y diversas tiendas de mercaderes. Al cruzar bajo los arcos de piedra desde el Valle de los Héroes, los viajeros acceden directamente al Distrito de Mercaderes. Esta vibrante plaza abierta actúa como el principal mercado y centro logístico de Ventormenta. En su centro se erige la Casa de Subastas, flanqueada cerca por el Banco de Ventormenta —el banco principal de la ciudad— y la popular taberna conocida como La Rosa Áurea. El distrito conecta directamente el enclave militar del Casco Antiguo, la serena Plaza de la Catedral y las arcanas avenidas del Barrio de los Magos, asegurando que las monedas, las materias primas y los suministros para la aventura circulen con rapidez por el reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, the Trade District is the quintessential hub for banking, trading at the Auction House, organizing guilds, and taking flight across the Eastern Kingdoms."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Trade District sits just past the city's main entrance gates and the Valley of Heroes. It connects directly to Cathedral Square to the northwest, Old Town to the east, and the Mage Quarter across the canals to the southwest.",["al"]={"trade district location","where is trade district","how to get to trade district"},["q"]="Where is the Trade District located?"},{["a"]="The Stormwind Counting House (the primary city bank) and The Gilded Rose inn are situated along the southwest perimeter of the Trade District, directly convenient to the main thoroughfare.",["al"]={"trade district bank","gilded rose location","stormwind bank trade district"},["q"]="Where can I find the bank and the inn?"},{["a"]="The Stormwind Visitor's Center, located on your left immediately upon entering the Trade District from the city gates, houses the Guild Master and tabard design services.",["al"]={"guild master stormwind","guild registrar","make a guild"},["q"]="Where do I register a guild or design a tabard in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="A stone ramp on the eastern side of the Trade District leads directly up to the Gryphon Roost, where the flight master dispatches gryphons across the kingdom and beyond.",["al"]={"flight master stormwind","gryphon roost stormwind","where is flight master"},["q"]="Where can I take a gryphon flight from the Trade District?"}},["kw"]={"auction house","bazaar","counting house","gilded rose","gryphon roost","stormwind","trade district","visitor center"},["n"]="Trade District",["s"]="The Trade District is the bustling commercial heart of Stormwind City, located immediately past the main gates and the Valley of Heroes. It serves as the primary hub for adventurers and citizens alike, housing the city's central bank, auction house, guild registry, and diverse merchant shops.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Crossing beneath the stone arches from the Valley of Heroes brings travelers directly into the Trade District. This vibrant open plaza acts as Stormwind's primary marketplace and logistical hub. At its center stands the Auction House, flanked nearby by the Stormwind Counting House, the city's main bank, and the popular tavern known as The Gilded Rose. The district directly bridges the gap between the military enclave of Old Town, the serene Cathedral Square, and the arcane avenues of the Mage Quarter, ensuring that coin, raw goods, and adventuring supplies circulate swiftly through the realm.",["t"]="The Crossroads of Commerce"},{["b"]="Every essential commodity can be acquired along the paved avenues and flanking canals. Weapon smiths at Weller's Arsenal and Lionheart Armory supply blades and mail, fletchers peddle bows at The Empty Quiver, and artisanal stalls offer everything from fresh flowers to fine aged vintages from the Gallina Winery. Just inside the gates, the Stormwind Visitor's Center coordinates newly registered charters and tabard designs for organized adventuring guilds, while an elevated ramp on the eastern side climbs toward the Gryphon Roost, linking the capital's mercantile life to the rest of the Alliance territories.",["t"]="Bazaars and Guild Halls"}}}}}
t["subzone:trade-quarter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,354,19.694.0,35.206.0,45.214.0,33.269.0,46.212.0",["h"]="18c4dd",["n"]="Barrio del Comercio",["s"]="Barrio del Comercio. El Barrio del Comercio forma el núcleo central de Entrañas, situado directamente bajo los elevadores de las Ruinas de Lordaeron. Funciona como el palpitante corazón económico de los Renegados, albergando sus principales cámaras bancarias, la casa de subastas y servicios cívicos esenciales. Desde este centro concéntrico, pasillos abovedados se ramifican hacia los distritos circundantes. Al descender desde la devastada superficie de Lordaeron, los viajeros bajan de los elevadores para adentrarse en la resonante extensión de piedra del Barrio del Comercio. Diseñado con una disposición circular escalonada, su plataforma central alberga las arcas de la ciudad y el banco central, enmarcado por puentes que cruzan canales de efluvios nocivos. Las terrazas circundantes bullen de vendedores, registros de hermandades y subastadores que regatean en medio de una penumbra inquietante. Incluso los alojamientos más básicos reflejan el pragmatismo de los Renegados: la posada local ofrece ataúdes de madera sin forrar en lugar de camas blandas. Desde este nexo central, arcadas de piedra conducen hacia los barrios especializados de la ciudad, convirtiéndolo en el cruce de caminos inevitable para cualquier negocio que se lleve a cabo en la capital.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="For Orc, Tauren, or Troll emissaries arriving in Tirisfal Glades, the Trade Quarter serves as the foreign, shadowy market center of their northern allies.",["race:Undead"]="The Trade Quarter represents the swift reclamation of civilized order by the Forsaken, turning subterranean dungeons into a thriving market dedicated to funding their survival."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Trade Quarter occupies the dead center of the Undercity. When entering the capital via the surface elevators beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron, you step out immediately onto the upper ring of the district.",["al"]={"trade quarter location","how to find trade quarter","where is trade quarter"},["q"]="Where is the Trade Quarter located?"},{["a"]="The district hosts the central Undercity bank, an auction house along the outer ring, the primary inn, a bat handler for air travel, guild registrars, and various trade trainers including the city's cooking mentor.",["al"]={"trade quarter services","what is in trade quarter","undercity bank location"},["q"]="What services are found in the Trade Quarter?"},{["a"]="Forsaken physiology requires no true sleep, and many retain habits suited to their undead condition. The inn provides plain, unlined wooden caskets rather than traditional bedding—a matter of routine comfort for the dead, though deeply unsettling for living visitors.",["al"]={"undercity inn coffins","why caskets in inn","undercity beds"},["q"]="Why are there coffins in the inn?"},{["a"]="Jeremiah Payson makes his living under one of the central bridges crossing into the bank. While standard merchants peddle weaponry and trade goods up above, Payson sells live pet cockroaches to curious passersby.",["al"]={"jeremiah payson","cockroach guy undercity","who sells cockroaches"},["q"]="Who is the vendor lurking beneath the bridges?"}},["kw"]={"auction house","bank","bat handler","caskets","inn","jeremiah payson","trade quarter","undercity"},["n"]="Trade Quarter",["s"]="The Trade Quarter forms the central core of the Undercity, resting directly beneath the lifts from the Ruins of Lordaeron. It functions as the beating economic heart of the Forsaken, housing their primary bank vaults, auction market, and essential civic services. From this concentric hub, vaulted corridors branch outward into the surrounding districts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Descending from the shattered surface of Lordaeron, travelers step off the lifts into the echoing stone expanse of the Trade Quarter. Designed around a tiered, circular layout, its central platform holds the city coffers and central bank, framed by bridges spanning noxious runoff canals. Surrounding terraces buzz with vendors, guild registries, and auctioneers bargaining amidst the eerie gloom. Even basic accommodations reflect Forsaken pragmatism: the local inn offers unlined wooden caskets rather than soft beds. From this central nexus, stone archways lead outward into the city's specialized quarters, making it the unavoidable crossroads for any business conducted within the capital.",["t"]="Heart of the Crypts"}}}}}
t["subzone:tradesmen-s-terrace"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,370,31.671.0,20.467.0,28.216.0,40.158.0,45.140.0,49.169.0",["h"]="64da90",["n"]="Bancal de los Mercaderes",["s"]="Bancal de los Mercaderes. El Bancal de los Mercaderes es el bullicioso corazón comercial de Darnassus, situado a lo largo del flanco sur de la ciudad. Reúne a artesanos, comerciantes y la casa de subastas local bajo la amplia arquitectura de madera de la capital de los elfos de la noche. El bancal sirve como el principal nexo comercial que conecta a los artesanos con los aventureros que viajan por Teldrassil y más allá. Ocupando la franja sur de Darnassus, el Bancal de los Mercaderes alberga la vida mercantil de la capital. Mientras que gran parte de la ciudad está dedicada a la contemplación silenciosa, los santuarios de naturaleza salvaje y los deberes espirituales, este bancal congrega a tenderos, artesanos y comerciantes que atienden tanto a los kaldorei locales como a viajeros de toda la Alianza. Contiene la casa de subastas central de Darnassus, provisiones generales y tiendas de suministros para profesiones, lo que lo convierte en el punto de partida esencial para los viajes por la naturaleza. Amplios senderos lo conectan hacia el norte directamente con el Bancal del Guerrero y hacia el oeste con las serenas aguas de Los Jardines del Templo y el grandioso Templo de la Luna.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The terrace offers Alliance travelers coming through Rut'theran Village access to banking, auctioneers, and essential trade supplies before heading deeper into Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, Tradesmen's Terrace is a rare center of dense urban commerce, adapted to preserve the peaceful canopy of Darnassus without the disruptive industry of other races."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tradesmen's Terrace is the southern marketplace district of Darnassus. It serves as the commercial center for the night elven capital, containing most of the city's merchants, artisans, and its central auction house.",["al"]={"what is this place","tradesmens terrace info","tradesmen terrace darnassus"},["q"]="What is Tradesmen's Terrace?"},{["a"]="The Darnassus auction house is located right here in Tradesmen's Terrace. It provides travelers, traders, and locals access to citywide and Alliance commerce.",["al"]={"darnassus auction house","ah location darnassus","where is ah"},["q"]="Where is the auction house in Darnassus?"},{["a"]="Paths from Tradesmen's Terrace lead north into the Warrior's Terrace and west toward the Temple Gardens and the towering Temple of the Moon.",["al"]={"exits from tradesmens terrace","where does this terrace lead","how to leave tradesmens terrace"},["q"]="How do I reach the other districts from here?"},{["a"]="The terrace hosts a broad variety of general merchants, trade supply vendors, and craftspeople catering to everyday needs, repairs, and goods produced across Teldrassil.",["al"]={"vendors tradesmens terrace","what can i buy here","tradesmen shops"},["q"]="What kinds of vendors are found in this district?"}},["kw"]={"auction house","darnassus","kaldorei","merchants","shops","teldrassil","tradesmen's terrace","vendors"},["n"]="Tradesmen's Terrace",["s"]="Tradesmen's Terrace is the bustling commercial heart of Darnassus, situated along the city's southern flank. It brings together craftspeople, merchants, and the local auction house beneath the sweeping wooden architecture of the night elf capital. The terrace serves as the primary trade link connecting artisans with adventurers journeying across Teldrassil and beyond.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Occupying the southern stretch of Darnassus, Tradesmen's Terrace houses the capital's mercantile life. While much of the city is devoted to quiet contemplation, wilderness sanctuaries, and spiritual duties, this terrace brings together shopkeepers, tradespeople, and merchants serving both local kaldorei and travelers from the wider Alliance. It contains Darnassus's central auction house, general provisions, and crafting supply stores, making it the essential staging ground for journeys into the wilds. Broad footpaths connect it northward directly to the Warrior's Terrace and westward toward the serene waters of the Temple Gardens and the grand Temple of the Moon.",["t"]="The Commercial Hub of Darnassus"},{["b"]="Kaldorei crafts prioritize harmony with nature, and the shops here reflect that delicate balance. Even amidst everyday commerce, the terrace operates without the roaring furnaces or smog seen in dwarven or human workshops, favoring quiet stone, curated timber, and woven goods. For visiting adventurers seeking trade contracts, repairs, or materials gathered from Teldrassil's dense boughs, the terrace stands as the principal center of business in northern Kalimdor.",["t"]="Artisans and Traders"}}}}}
t["subzone:train-depot"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,222,20.566.0,33.171.0,43.153.0,45.154.0,33.145.0",["h"]="8c79ea",["n"]="Estación de Trenes",["s"]="Estación de Trenes. La Estación de Trenes es un nudo de transporte subterráneo situado justo debajo de las entradas de superficie de Gnomeregan en Dun Morogh. Antaño un bullicioso centro de locomoción gnómica, ahora está plagado de hostiles gnomos parias y troggs invasores. Situada en el fondo del gran ascensor que baja desde Dun Morogh, la Estación de Trenes sirvió en su día como el nexo principal para el transporte ferroviario por toda la maravilla subterránea de Gnomeregan. En la actualidad, los andenes y las vías yacen en ruinas. La radiación que contaminó la ciudad transformó a los trabajadores restantes en enloquecidos gnomos parias, mientras que los troggs subterráneos han invadido las vías. Los exploradores que descienden a la ciudad en ruinas deben sortear esta zona preliminar para llegar a sectores más profundos como Corredor Mecánico, la Sala de Carga y las instalaciones interiores de ingeniería.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers seeking rare schematics often scout the depot's lower platforms, where surviving gnome peddlers like Namdo Bizzfizzle still ply their trade amidst the wreckage.",["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes, the abandoned depot is a tragic sight, showing the ruin of the advanced locomotion systems that once united their subterranean metropolis."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Train Depot lies directly beneath the surface entrance elevator in Dun Morogh, acting as one of the outer threshold areas before venturing into the core of Gnomeregan.",["al"]={"train depot location","how to get to train depot","train depot entrance"},["q"]="Where is the Train Depot located?"},{["a"]="The depot is overrun by feral troggs who burrowed up from the deep earth and wretched leper gnomes who lost their sanity during the radioactive disaster.",["al"]={"train depot enemies","mobs in train depot","who is in train depot"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit the Train Depot now?"},{["a"]="Passages lead west into Clockwerk Run and toward the Loading Room, while a northern workshop area houses a back door down into the upper Engineering Labs.",["al"]={"train depot exits","where does train depot go","train depot connections"},["q"]="Where do the paths from the Train Depot lead?"},{["a"]="Namdo Bizzfizzle, an engineering supplier, manages to survive tucked away beneath the north side of the main platform on the depot's lower level.",["al"]={"namdo bizzfizzle","train depot npc","train depot vendor"},["q"]="Who is hiding in the Train Depot?"}},["kw"]={"clockwerk run","dun morogh","gnomeregan","leper gnome","loading room","namdo bizzfizzle","train depot","trogg"},["n"]="Train Depot",["s"]="The Train Depot is a subterranean transit hub located just below the surface entrances of Gnomeregan in Dun Morogh. Once a bustling center of gnomish locomotion, it now swarms with hostile leper gnomes and invading troggs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated at the bottom of the grand elevator leading down from Dun Morogh, the Train Depot once served as the primary nexus for rail transport across the subterranean marvel of Gnomeregan. Today, the platforms and railbeds lie in shambles. The fallout that irradiated the city transformed its remaining workers into crazed leper gnomes, while subterranean troggs have overrun the tracks. Explorers descending into the ruined city must navigate this staging ground to reach deeper sectors such as Clockwerk Run, the Loading Room, and the inner engineering facilities.",["t"]="A Ruined Transit Hub"}}}}}
t["subzone:tundrid-hills"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,232,24.401.0,36.205.0,50.237.0,47.126.0",["h"]="acec88",["n"]="Las Colinas Tundra",["s"]="Las Colinas Tundra. Las Colinas Tundra son un tramo escarpado y cubierto de nieve de tierras altas en el centro-sur de Dun Morogh, situado justo al oeste de la Cantera de Gol'Bolar. Habitados por una peligrosa fauna de montaña, los pasos rocosos rara vez son transitados por viajeros ocasionales. Extendiéndose entre el Valle de Crestanevada y las tierras bajas del este de Dun Morogh, las Colinas Tundra ofrecen una ruta escarpada a través del campo para aquellos que buscan evitar los caminos principales que pasan por Kharanos. Sin embargo, la comodidad tiene un precio muy alto. Las escarpadas laderas nevadas están acechadas por feroces depredadores, lo que convierte el territorio en un lugar peligroso para los viajeros desprevenidos que se aventuran fuera del camino trillado sin un arma en la mano.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The wind-battered crags provide rugged tracking grounds filled with hardy beasts adapted to Dun Morogh's punishing mountain chill.",["race:Dwarf"]="For mountaineers of Ironforge, these heights serve as an ever-present reminder that wilderness and hostile Frostmane trolls press close against Dun Morogh's heartland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Tundrid Hills span the south-central portion of Dun Morogh, positioned west of the Gol'Bolar Quarry and forming a natural, elevated boundary south of the main road connecting Kharanos to eastern lands.",["al"]={"tundrid hills location","where is tundrid hills","tundrid hills map"},["q"]="Where are the Tundrid Hills located?"},{["a"]="Adventurers sometimes navigate these harsh ridges as an overland shortcut between Coldridge Valley and eastern Dun Morogh, bypassing the established settlement routes, though it is far more hazardous than sticking to the patrolled roads.",["al"]={"why go to tundrid hills","tundrid hills shortcut"},["q"]="Why would anyone travel through the Tundrid Hills?"},{["a"]="The hills are home to fierce native wildlife accustomed to the freezing heights, and few travel here without a weapon at hand.",["al"]={"what lives here","tundrid hills enemies","monsters in tundrid hills"},["q"]="What threats can be found in the Tundrid Hills?"}},["kw"]={"coldridge valley","dun morogh","frostmane","gol'bolar quarry","ironforge","kharanos","tundrid hills"},["n"]="Tundrid Hills",["s"]="The Tundrid Hills are a rugged, snowbound stretch of highland in south-central Dun Morogh, lying just west of the Gol'Bolar Quarry. Inhabited by dangerous mountain wildlife, the rocky passes are rarely traversed by casual travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching between Coldridge Valley and the lowlands of eastern Dun Morogh, the Tundrid Hills offer a rugged cross-country route for those looking to bypass the main roads through Kharanos. However, convenience comes at a steep price. The jagged snowy slopes are prowled by ferocious predators, making the territory perilous for unwary travelers who venture off the beaten path without a drawn weapon.",["t"]="A Treacherous Wilderness"}}}}}
t["subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="26,345,23.464.0,36.214.0,51.187.0,34.200.0",["h"]="5b8c99",["n"]="Orilla Crepuscular (Costa Oscura)",["s"]="Orilla Crepuscular (Costa Oscura). La Orilla Crepuscular es un escarpado tramo de costa en el sur de Costa Oscura que se extiende hacia el sur desde la Playa del Oleaje hasta la frontera con Vallefresno. Sus playas sombrías y cubiertas de niebla están interrumpidas por acantilados marinos salientes, islotes y un oleaje traicionero. La zona está infestada de tribus de múrlocs agresivos y voraces depredadores acuáticos como los trilladones. Extendiéndose al sur de la Playa del Oleaje más allá de las ruinas de Ameth'Aran hacia Vallefresno, la Orilla Crepuscular es una de las partes más escarpadas e inhóspitas de la costa de Costa Oscura. La arena gris da paso a acantilados afilados y azotados por las olas, así como a islas rocosas dispersas. Las aguas de la zona son notablemente hostiles; nadar cerca de la costa invita al ataque de trilladones territoriales y reptadores marinos, mientras que las propias playas están dominadas por prósperos campamentos de múrlocs agresivos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:NightElf"]="The Twilight Shore marks the lonely, mist-shrouded threshold between the haunted ruins of Darkshore and the sacred ancestral forests of Ashenvale."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It encompasses the southernmost coastal strip of Darkshore, beginning south of the Long Wash (roughly west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran) and continuing southward until reaching the rocky borders of Ashenvale.",["al"]={"twilight shore location","where is twilight shore","twilight shore map"},["q"]="Where is the Twilight Shore located?"},{["a"]="The shoreline is heavily settled by aggressive murloc tribes, while the surrounding cold surf is home to territorial threshadons, lurkers, and giant crabs that prey upon unwary travelers.",["al"]={"twilight shore mobs","dangers at twilight shore","what is at twilight shore"},["q"]="What threats can be found along the Twilight Shore?"},{["a"]="Unlike the flatter, expansive beaches farther north, the Twilight Shore is fragmented by sharp sea cliffs, rocky shoals, and small offshore islands shaped by the relentless pounding of the Veiled Sea.",["al"]={"why are there cliffs","twilight shore geography"},["q"]="Why is the terrain so rugged here?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","coast","darkshore","long wash","murlocs","threshadons","twilight shore"},["n"]="Twilight Shore (Darkshore)",["s"]="The Twilight Shore is a rugged stretch of coast in southern Darkshore, running south from the Long Wash down to the border of Ashenvale. Its gloomy, mist-laden beaches are interrupted by jutting sea cliffs, offshore islets, and treacherous surf. The area is infested with aggressive murloc tribes and ravenous aquatic predators like threshadons.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching south of the Long Wash past the ruins of Ameth'Aran toward Ashenvale, the Twilight Shore is among the most rugged and inhospitable parts of Darkshore's coastline. Gray sand gives way to sharp, wave-battered cliffs and scattered rocky islands. The waters here are notoriously hostile; swimming off the coast invites attacks from territorial threshadons and sea crawlers, while the beaches themselves are dominated by thriving camps of aggressive murlocs.",["t"]="A Treacherous Coastline"}}}}}
t["subzone:twilight-vale"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,357,20.517.0,35.178.0,32.199.0,38.220.0,42.220.0",["h"]="6726e9",["n"]="Vega Crepuscular",["s"]="Vega Crepuscular. La Vega Crepuscular abarca los densos y sombríos bosques meridionales de Costa Oscura, que se extienden hacia la frontera con Vallefresno. Bajo su penumbra, fúrbolgs corruptos, osos rabiosos y feroces sables de la noche merodean por la maleza, haciendo que viajar campo a través sea sumamente peligroso. Sirve como un lúgubre umbral entre la costa mancillada de Costa Oscura y las copas sagradas del sur. Extendiéndose desde el sur de las antiguas ruinas de Ameth'Aran hasta la frontera con Vallefresno, la Vega Crepuscular cubre los confines meridionales de Costa Oscura en un anochecer perpetuo. La corrupción invasora que asola el norte de Kalimdor ha hecho mella profunda en la fauna local. Osos rabiosos vagan junto a sables de la noche feroces, y tribus hostiles de fúrbolgs acechan en el oscuro bosque. Tanto las centinelas como los viajeros aconsejan ceñirse estrictamente al camino principal, ya que desviarse tan solo unos pasos entre los árboles invita a sufrir emboscadas rápidas y letales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids passing between Darkshore and Ashenvale witness firsthand the sickness afflicting the vale's creatures, underscoring the urgent need to cleanse the land.",["race:NightElf"]="The degradation of the southern woods weighs heavily on the night elves, who mourn the corruption of the native beasts and the fall of their furbolg neighbors so close to Ashenvale's threshold."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Twilight Vale forms the southern portion of Darkshore. It begins just south of the highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran and extends all the way to the border pass that enters Ashenvale.",["al"]={"twilight vale location","where is twilight vale","twilight vale map"},["q"]="Where is the Twilight Vale located?"},{["a"]="The vale is infested with afflicted wildlife and hostile tribes. Travelers will encounter rabid bears, aggressive nightsabers, and corrupted furbolgs who attack anyone intruding upon their territory.",["al"]={"twilight vale monsters","what is in twilight vale","danger twilight vale"},["q"]="What threats wander this forest?"},{["a"]="No wilderness in Darkshore is entirely safe, but sticking firmly to the established dirt road is far safer than cutting through the underbrush. Straying off the beaten track puts you directly in the path of feral beasts.",["al"]={"is twilight vale safe","safe path darkshore to ashenvale"},["q"]="Is it safe to travel through the vale?"},{["a"]="Darkshore has suffered heavily since the Third War and the sundering magic lingering across northern Kalimdor. Tainted water and dark magical residue have maddened the local wildlife and turned peaceful furbolgs violent.",["al"]={"why are bears rabid in darkshore","furbolg corruption twilight vale"},["q"]="Why is the wildlife in the vale corrupted?"}},["kw"]={"ameth'aran","ashenvale","darkshore","furbolgs","nightsabers","rabid bears","twilight vale"},["n"]="Twilight Vale",["s"]="Twilight Vale encompasses the dense, shadowed southern woodlands of Darkshore stretching toward the Ashenvale border. Beneath its gloom, corrupted furbolgs, rabid bears, and vicious nightsabers prowl the undergrowth, making off-road passage perilous. It serves as a grim threshold between the tainted coast of Darkshore and the sacred canopies to the south.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running from the south of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran all the way to the border of Ashenvale, the Twilight Vale blankets the southern reaches of Darkshore in perpetual dusk. The encroaching corruption plaguing northern Kalimdor has bitten deep into the wildlife here. Rabid bears roam alongside feral nightsabers, and hostile furbolg tribes stalk the dark wood. Sentinels and travelers alike advise sticking strictly to the main road, as straying even a few paces into the trees invites swift and deadly ambushes.",["t"]="A Perilous Threshold"}}}}}
t["subzone:valgan-s-field"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,230,18.546.0,15.210.0,38.231.0,45.200.0,39.157.0",["h"]="a5bc92",["n"]="Campo de Valgan",["s"]="Campo de Valgan. El Campo de Valgan es una granja de trigo abandonada situada en el norte de Bosque de Argénteos, con vistas al Lago Lordamere. Antaño una pintoresca hacienda, ahora yace desolada e invadida por los feroces huargen Furia Lunar desatados por el archimago Arugal. Situado justo al oeste de La Playa Plateada y al norte del río cercano, el Campo de Valgan fue en su momento una próspera granja de trigo con vistas panorámicas al Lago Lordamere. Esa pacífica vida se desvaneció cuando la Plaga arrasó Lordaeron, obligando a su dueño, Valgan, a huir o encontrar su fin. Sin nadie a su cuidado, las estructuras en ruinas cayeron en las garras de los feroces huargen Furia Lunar que bajaban merodeando desde el Castillo de Colmillo Oscuro. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, el mago Arugal pasó un tiempo aquí, dejando tras de sí restos de sus investigaciones arcanas que ahora llaman la atención de los Renegados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Arugal's abandoned research at the farm offers a sobering warning of the catastrophic perils of unchecked summoning and extraplanar magic.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, clearing Valgan's Field is essential to securing the road through Silverpine and recovering Arugal's notes before his monstrous pets spread further north."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Valgan was the human farmer who owned and worked this homestead before the Third War. When the Scourge swept across northern Lordaeron, Valgan either died or fled into exile, leaving the farm to fall into ruin.",["al"]={"valgan","who is valgan","valgans field history"},["q"]="Who was Valgan?"},{["a"]="The feral Moonrage pack infesting the farm was summoned into Silverpine Forest by Archmage Arugal. Arugal unleashed the beasts against the Scourge, but quickly lost control as they spread across the forest, and guilt drove him mad.",["al"]={"why are there worgen here","moonrage worgen valgan","who brought the worgen"},["q"]="Why are worgen roaming Valgan's Field?"},{["a"]="Archmage Arugal resided at the farm before the war and left behind valuable spellbooks. The Forsaken seek out these lost writings in their campaign to understand and counter Arugal's terrifying magic.",["al"]={"valgans field quest","why forsaken care about valgans field","arugal spellbook farm"},["q"]="Why are the Forsaken interested in this farm?"},{["a"]="Aside from the packs of Moonrage worgen haunting the fields, a dangerous beast known as Nightlash is occasionally spotted prowling the surrounding perimeter.",["al"]={"nightlash","rare spawn valgans field","monsters at valgan"},["q"]="What rare threats appear near the farm?"}},["kw"]={"arugal","moonrage","nightlash","shining strand","silverpine forest","valgan","valgan's field","worgen"},["n"]="Valgan's Field",["s"]="Valgan's Field is an abandoned wheat farm nestled in northern Silverpine Forest, overlooking Lordamere Lake. Once a picturesque homestead, it now lies desolate and overrun by the feral Moonrage worgen unleashed by Archmage Arugal.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated just west of the Shining Strand and north of the nearby river, Valgan's Field was once a prosperous wheat farm offering scenic views of Lordamere Lake. That peaceful life vanished when the Scourge tore through Lordaeron, forcing its owner, Valgan, to flee or meet his end. Left untended, the ruined structures fell into the claws of feral Moonrage worgen prowling down from Shadowfang Keep. Before the Third War, the mage Arugal spent time here, leaving behind remnants of his arcane research that now draw the attention of the Forsaken.",["t"]="A Ruined Homestead"}}}}}
t["subzone:valley-of-heroes"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,306,22.531.0,16.488.0,36.259.0,49.242.0,50.219.0,37.175.0",["h"]="cd3218",["n"]="Valle de los Héroes",["s"]="Valle de los Héroes. El Valle de los Héroes conforma la monumental entrada sur a Ciudad de Ventormenta, llevando a los viajeros por un puente de piedra que cruza el foso. Flanqueado por imponentes estatuas en honor a los líderes de la Alianza en su expedición a Draenor, sirve tanto de sobrecogedora bienvenida como de puesto de control fuertemente fortificado. Erigidas durante la gran reconstrucción de Ventormenta tras la Segunda Guerra, las estatuas que bordean la calzada conmemoran a los comandantes de la expedición de la Alianza. Estos campeones cruzaron El Portal Oscuro hacia el mundo natal de los orcos, Draenor, para sellar la brecha para siempre, dando sus vidas para que Azeroth pudiera sobrevivir. Los visitantes que avanzan hacia el norte en dirección al Distrito de Mercaderes pasan bajo los rostros del archimago Khadgar, Kurdran Martillo Salvaje, la capitana forestal Alleria Brisaveloz, el comandante en jefe Danath Aterratrols y el alto general Turalyon.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="The statue of General Turalyon stands as a profound inspiration to paladins, immortalizing one of the original champions of the Knights of the Silver Hand.",["faction:Alliance"]="Every citizen of the Grand Alliance reveres the valley as a solemn testament to racial cooperation, honoring human, high elven, and dwarven martyrs side by side."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The five colossal monuments depict the legendary commanders of the Sons of Lothar who led the Alliance Expedition to Draenor: High General Turalyon, Ranger-Captain Alleria Windrunner, Archmage Khadgar, Kurdran Wildhammer, and Force Commander Danath Trollbane.",["al"]={"statues in stormwind","who are the heroes","valley statues","names on statues"},["q"]="Who are the statues lining the path?"},{["a"]="Constructed during the city's restoration after the Second War, the statues serve as an enduring tribute to the heroes assumed lost during the destruction of Draenor. They remind all who enter of the steep price paid to keep the kingdom safe.",["al"]={"why build statues here","valley of heroes purpose"},["q"]="Why were these monuments placed at the city gate?"},{["a"]="General Marcus Jonathan, the supreme commander of the Stormwind City Guard, oversees the security of the valley directly from the front lines, supported by officers such as Major Mattingly and Field Marshal Stonebridge.",["al"]={"guard captain","who is the guy on the horse","who leads stormwind defense"},["q"]="Who commands the guards stationed at the entrance?"},{["a"]="Heading north over the bridge brings travelers directly into Stormwind City's bustling Trade District, while heading south exits the gates into the pastoral forests of Elwynn.",["al"]={"where does bridge go","directions stormwind gate"},["q"]="Where does the Valley of Heroes lead?"}},["kw"]={"alleria","danath","khadgar","kurdran","marcus jonathan","stormwind gate","turalyon","valley of heroes"},["n"]="Valley of Heroes",["s"]="The Valley of Heroes forms the monumental southern entrance to Stormwind City, carrying travellers across a stone bridge spanning the moat. Flanked by towering statues honoring the leaders of the Alliance Expedition to Draenor, it serves as both an awe-inspiring welcome and a heavily fortified checkpoint.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Erected during the grand rebuilding of Stormwind following the Second War, the statues lining the causeway commemorate the commanders of the Alliance Expedition. These champions marched through the Dark Portal into the orcish homeworld of Draenor to seal the rift forever, giving their lives so Azeroth might survive. Visitors proceeding north toward the Trade District pass beneath the visages of Archmage Khadgar, Kurdran Wildhammer, Ranger-Captain Alleria Windrunner, Force Commander Danath Trollbane, and High General Turalyon.",["t"]="A Monument to the Lost"},{["b"]="Beyond its ceremonial role, the valley is the primary defensive choke point guarding Stormwind from overland invasion. The approaches are overseen by General Marcus Jonathan, commander of the city guard, who monitors all traffic entering and departing through the great gates astride his steed. Flanking commanders, including Major Mattingly and Field Marshal Stonebridge, maintain vigilance alongside rows of seasoned guards, ensuring the capital remains secure against external threats.",["t"]="The City Bastion"}}}}}
t["subzone:valley-of-honor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,383,26.559.0,25.391.0,43.206.0,44.187.0,52.169.0,26.160.0",["h"]="54088d",["n"]="Valle del Honor",["s"]="Valle del Honor. El Valle del Honor sirve como el núcleo marcial y distrito de guerreros de Orgrimmar, enclavado en los cañones del noreste de la capital. Alberga los cuarteles de la ciudad, las hermandades de guerreros y cazadores, y los maestros de batalla que dirigen a las fuerzas de la Horda por todo Azeroth. Con forjas activas, fosos de instrucción y aguas tranquilas, es el lugar donde la Horda perfecciona su fuerza y recuerda su legado marcial. Situado tras las altas crestas del cañón, el Valle del Honor actúa como el principal barrio militar de Orgrimmar. Aquí, el entrechocar de las armas de práctica y el tintineo de los yunques de herrería marcan el día a día. La Sala de los Valientes domina el valle, sirviendo como punto de encuentro para guerreros veteranos y maestros de batalla que coordinan campañas en frentes como el Valle de Alterac y la Garganta Grito de Guerra. Flanqueado por instalaciones de instrucción para maestros de bestias y cazadores, el distrito está dedicado por completo a equipar, adiestrar y movilizar a los defensores de primera línea de la Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The Hunter's Hall and beast-taming grounds make this valley an essential stop for replenishing ammunition, honing marksmanship, and stabling companions.",["class:Warrior"]="The Valley of Honor is your spiritual home in Orgrimmar, housing the Hall of the Brave, veteran combat instructors, and the armorers who forge the Horde's front lines."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the military and martial hub of Orgrimmar. It contains the city's barracks, warrior and hunter trainers, weaponsmiths, and the battlemasters responsible for dispatching soldiers to major battlefronts.",["al"]={"valley of honor purpose","what is here","what's in valley of honor"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Valley of Honor?"},{["a"]="The Horde battlemasters are stationed inside the Hall of the Brave, located in the Valley of Honor. From there, soldiers are enlisted and dispatched to ongoing engagements across Azeroth.",["al"]={"battlemaster location","orgrimmar pvp","queue bg orgrimmar"},["q"]="Where can I find battlemasters in Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="The valley is home to trainers and supply vendors for blacksmithing, mining, and fishing, along with goblin engineering specialists operating out of Nogg's Machine Shop.",["al"]={"professions valley of honor","trainers here","blacksmithing orgrimmar"},["q"]="What professions are trained in the Valley of Honor?"},{["a"]="The Wyvern's Tail is the local tavern and inn situated along the edge of the valley, providing food, drink, and rest for weary warriors, hunters, and travelers.",["al"]={"wyverns tail","inn in valley of honor","valley of honor tavern"},["q"]="What is The Wyvern's Tail?"}},["kw"]={"barracks","battlemasters","blacksmithing","hall of the brave","nogg","orgrimmar","the wyvern's tail","valley of honor"},["n"]="Valley of Honor",["s"]="The Valley of Honor serves as the martial core and warrior district of Orgrimmar, nestled in the northeastern canyons of the capital. It houses the city's barracks, warrior and hunter guilds, and the battlemasters directing Horde forces across Azeroth. With active forges, training rings, and quiet waters, it is where the Horde hones its strength and remembers its martial heritage.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated behind high canyon ridges, the Valley of Honor acts as Orgrimmar's primary military quarter. Here, the clatter of practice weaponry and the ringing of blacksmith anvils define daily life. The Hall of the Brave dominates the valley, serving as a gathering point for seasoned warriors and battlemasters coordinating campaigns across battlefronts like Alterac Valley and Warsong Gulch. Flanked by training facilities for beastmasters and hunters, the district is dedicated entirely to equipping, drilling, and mobilizing the Horde's frontline defenders.",["t"]="Heart of the Horde's Might"},{["b"]="Beyond arms and drill grounds, the valley supports the logistics of war. The Burning Anvil and Red Canyon Mining supply armor and raw iron, while engineers tinker nearby in Nogg's Machine Shop. Between duties, grunts and visiting adventurers cast a line into the valley's surprisingly serene secluded pool, offering brief moments of calm away from the dusty bustle of the Valley of Strength.",["t"]="Craft, Trade, and Respite"}}}}}
t["subzone:valley-of-kings"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,419,30.518.0,29.508.0,39.257.0,40.286.0,57.257.0,28.206.0",["h"]="eb5ccf",["n"]="Valle de los Reyes",["s"]="Valle de los Reyes. El Valle de los Reyes es un frondoso cañón situado en el rincón sudoccidental de Loch Modan, justo al sur del paso hacia Dun Morogh. Sirve como puerta de entrada fuertemente vigilada a la ardiente Garganta de Fuego, flanqueada por figuras monumentales de piedra esculpidas en memoria de la Guerra de los Tres Martillos. Los viajeros que se aventuran aquí caminan bajo la historia enana ancestral mientras afrontan la amenaza inmediata de los invasores Rocanegra y los troggs. El elemento más imponente del valle es la pareja de estatuas colosales que representan al rey Madoran Barbabronce y al Alto señor feudal Khardros Martillo Salvaje. Esculpidos por encargo conjunto de sus hijos tras sus muertes, estos titanes de piedra dominan el paso hacia las calcinadas tierras del sur. Se erigen como un monumento duradero a la victoria aliada en la Guerra de los Tres Martillos y una advertencia eterna contra el clan Hierro Negro, recordando a todos los que miran hacia el sur la ruina traída sobre las Montañas Crestagrana por la invocación de Ragnaros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The valley acts as the northern bulwark against the gathering threats of the Redridge badlands, keeping the smoldering perils of the Searing Gorge from spilling into peaceful Khaz Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, the Valley of Kings is hallowed ground showcasing the unbreakable bond forged between Bronzebeard and Wildhammer against the treachery of the Dark Irons."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The two immense statues depict King Madoran Bronzebeard of Ironforge and High Thane Khardros Wildhammer. Their sons commissioned the monuments together following their fathers' deaths to celebrate the alliance that triumphed in the War of the Three Hammers.",["al"]={"statues in valley of kings","dwarf statues loch modan","who are the statues"},["q"]="Who do the two giant statues represent?"},{["a"]="They were erected to gaze directly toward the southern territories shattered by the Dark Iron clan's summoning of Ragnaros. The twin kings stand as a protective shield and an enduring warning to the Dark Irons and any other hostile force attempting to invade the northern dwarven lands.",["al"]={"why statues look south","purpose of statues","statues facing searing gorge"},["q"]="Why were the statues built facing south?"},{["a"]="The gate leading into the Searing Gorge is kept locked for traveler safety. You must speak with Mountaineer Pebblebitty, who stands guard at the gate, and prove your capabilities by undertaking a task for her before she will provide the key to pass through.",["al"]={"how to open searing gorge gate","mountaineer pebblebitty key","valley of kings gate locked"},["q"]="How do I get through the locked gate at the southern end?"},{["a"]="The valley connects the South Gate Pass leading to Dun Morogh, the trogg-infested Stonesplinter Valley to the east, and the blazing badlands of the Searing Gorge through the heavily fortified southern gate.",["al"]={"valley of kings connections","where does valley go"},["q"]="Where does this valley lead?"}},["kw"]={"khardros wildhammer","loch modan","madoran bronzebeard","pebblebitty","searing gorge gate","valley of kings","war of the three hammers"},["n"]="Valley of Kings",["s"]="The Valley of Kings is a lush canyon nestled in the southwestern corner of Loch Modan, directly south of the passage to Dun Morogh. It serves as a heavily watched gateway into the fiery Searing Gorge, flanked by monumental stone figures carved in memory of the War of the Three Hammers. Travelers venturing here walk beneath ancient dwarven history while facing the immediate threat of Blackrock encroachers and troggs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The valley's most commanding feature is the pair of colossal statues depicting King Madoran Bronzebeard and High Thane Khardros Wildhammer. Carved by joint commission from their sons following their deaths, these stone titans overlook the pass into the scorched southlands. They stand as a lasting monument to the allied victory in the War of the Three Hammers and an eternal warning against the Dark Iron clan, reminding all who look south of the ruin brought upon the Redridge Mountains by the summoning of Ragnaros.",["t"]="Guardians of the Southern Pass"},{["b"]="Beyond serving as a path between South Gate Pass and Stonesplinter Valley, the Valley of Kings holds the heavy iron gate leading down into the Searing Gorge. Because of the hostile Blackrock orcs, Dark Iron dwarves, and volcanic hazards lurking on the other side, the gate is kept strictly locked and guarded by Ironforge mountaineers. Mountaineer Pebblebitty keeps watch over the threshold, turning away all but the hardiest adventurers who can prove they possess the strength to survive the inferno beyond.",["t"]="The Gate to the Searing Gorge"}}}}}
t["subzone:valley-of-spirits"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,303,24.453.0,20.401.0,35.238.0,31.199.0,42.204.0",["h"]="64a3c3",["n"]="Valle de los Espíritus",["s"]="Valle de los Espíritus. Enclavado contra los acantilados occidentales de Orgrimmar, Valle de los Espíritus actúa como la sede tradicional de la tribu Lanza Negra dentro de la capital de la Horda. Repleto de cabañas de paja, postes tiki y estanques serenos, ofrece un marcado contraste con la arquitectura orca circundante de piedra roja y hierro forjado. Extendiéndose hacia el oeste desde el bullicioso Valle de la Fuerza, Valle de los Espíritus es un enclave exuberante y tranquilo dedicado a los trols Lanza Negra. Cuando la tribu se asentó en Durotar junto a los orcos de Thrall, este rincón sosegado entre los riscos se convirtió en su punto de reunión urbano. Artesanos, espiritualistas y practicantes trols se congregan alrededor de sus puentes de madera y aguas serpenteantes, practicando sus artes lejos del calor seco de las avenidas principales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Herbalism"]="The quiet waterways and specialized lodges in the valley make it a prime hub in the city for gathering wisdom from local herbalist masters.",["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear tribe, this peaceful enclave provides a crucial piece of home and cultural identity within the towering red canyons of the orcish capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The valley is primarily home to the Darkspear trolls who settled in Durotar alongside the orcs. You will find their craftsmen, spiritual leaders, herbalists, and hunters here, living among distinct troll-style huts and carved tiki totems.",["al"]={"who lives here","valley of spirits inhabitants","trolls in orgrimmar"},["q"]="Who lives in the Valley of Spirits?"},{["a"]="The Talon Gate sits at the rear of the Valley of Spirits, functioning as the western exit of Orgrimmar. Passing through it leads directly into the Southfury River basin and the plains of the Barrens.",["al"]={"talon gate exit","back gate orgrimmar","valley of spirits gate"},["q"]="Where does the Talon Gate lead?"},{["a"]="The Valley of Spirits features trainers and merchants for herbalism, cooking, and various wilderness and magical disciplines, housed across notable structures such as the Spirit Lodge and Darkbriar Lodge.",["al"]={"trainers in valley of spirits","what is in valley of spirits"},["q"]="What services and trainers are found here?"}},["kw"]={"darkbriar lodge","darkspear","orgrimmar","spirit lodge","talon gate","trolls","valley of spirits"},["n"]="Valley of Spirits",["s"]="Tucked against the western cliffs of Orgrimmar, the Valley of Spirits serves as the long-standing seat of the Darkspear tribe within the Horde's capital. Filled with thatched lodges, tiki poles, and serene pools, it offers a stark contrast to the surrounding red stone and iron-clad orcish architecture.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Branching westward off the bustling Valley of Strength, the Valley of Spirits is a lush and quiet enclave dedicated to the Darkspear trolls. When the tribe settled in Durotar alongside Thrall's orcs, this tranquil pocket among the crags became their urban gathering place. Trollish craftspeople, spiritualists, and practitioners gather around its wooden bridges and winding waters, practicing their arts away from the dry heat of the main thoroughfares.",["t"]="A Home for the Darkspear"},{["b"]="Beyond its dwellings and tranquil pools, the valley hosts practitioners of magic and wild crafts. Witch doctors, herbalists, and spellcasters congregate in lodges like the Spirit Lodge and Darkbriar Lodge. Tucked toward the back is the Talon Gate, which opens directly toward the open plains of the Barrens, offering quick passage for wanderers, hunters, and travelers roaming beyond the canyon walls.",["t"]="Keepers of the Craft"}}}}}
t["subzone:valley-of-strength"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,289,21.508.0,24.385.0,31.222.0,55.164.0,30.183.0,34.180.0",["h"]="746ece",["n"]="Valle de la Fuerza",["s"]="Valle de la Fuerza. El Valle de la Fuerza es la bulliciosa plaza central de Orgrimmar, que recibe a todos los que cruzan las imponentes puertas principales de la ciudad. Al albergar el banco de la ciudad, la casa de subastas central y la posada Colmillo Roto, sirve como el palpitante corazón comercial y administrativo de la capital de la Horda. Cruza las puertas fortificadas de madera de Orgrimmar y entrarás en el Valle de la Fuerza. Esculpido en lo profundo de la roca roja del cañón de Durotar, este valle sirve como la plaza principal de la Horda. Aventureros, comerciantes y guerreros de todas las naciones aliadas se mezclan en sus polvorientas plazas, compartiendo historias de guerra junto a jarras de la posada Colmillo Roto o atendiendo a intercambios vitales en el banco central y la casa de subastas. Es un bullicioso testimonio de la fuerza y la unidad que los orcos lucharon por establecer en su nuevo hogar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="As the primary plaza inside Orgrimmar's gates, the Valley of Strength is the first place Horde travelers meet to trade, recruit for expeditions."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the primary entryway and central valley of Orgrimmar, located just inside the city's main gates. It contains essential urban services such as the bank, auction house, general goods merchants, and the Broken Tusk inn.",["al"]={"valley of strength overview","what is this place","orgrimmar entrance area"},["q"]="What is the Valley of Strength?"},{["a"]="Grommash Hold is not in the Valley of Strength; it stands to the north in the Valley of Wisdom, serving as the seat of Warchief Thrall and the Horde's high command.",["al"]={"where is thrall","grommash hold location","warchief seat"},["q"]="Where is Grommash Hold located relative to this valley?"},{["a"]="The valley houses the city's primary bank, the auction house, trade supplies, armor merchants at Soran's Leather and Steel Armory, lodging at the Broken Tusk, and general trade goods.",["al"]={"valley of strength amenities","vendors valley of strength","what's here"},["q"]="What services can I find here?"},{["a"]="The valley is heavily patrolled by Orgrimmar Grunts, seasoned orc warriors who maintain peace, protect incoming caravans, and direct travelers through the labyrinthine canyon city.",["al"]={"orgrimmar grunts","guards in valley of strength","city defense"},["q"]="Who guards the Valley of Strength?"}},["kw"]={"auction house","bank","broken tusk","durotar","grommash hold","horde","orgrimmar","thrall","valley of strength"},["n"]="Valley of Strength",["s"]="The Valley of Strength is the bustling central commons of Orgrimmar, greeting all who pass through the city's towering front gates. Housing the city bank, the central auction house, and the Broken Tusk inn, it serves as the beating commercial and administrative heart of the Horde capital.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Step past the fortified timber gates of Orgrimmar and you enter the Valley of Strength. Carved deep into the red canyon rock of Durotar, this valley serves as the Horde's front square. Adventurers, merchants, and warriors from all allied nations mingle across its dusty plazas, swapping war stories over flagons from the Broken Tusk inn or attending to vital trade at the central bank and auction house. It is a bustling testament to the strength and unity the orcs fought to establish in their new homeland.",["t"]="The Gates of the City"},{["b"]="Beyond its defensive significance, the valley functions as the capital's foremost marketplace. Shops such as Soran's Leather and Steel Armory sell armor, while various vendors supply provisions for long treks across the Barrens. Grunts stand vigilant watch at every corner, directing newcomers and ensuring order among the diverse peoples who have taken refuge beneath Thrall's banner.",["t"]="Hub of Trade and Command"}}}}}
t["subzone:valley-of-trials"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="Es el campo de pruebas tradicional para los reclutas de la Horda, principalmente jóvenes orcos y trols Lanza Negra. En sus resguardados cañones, los nuevos aventureros completan rigurosas tareas para demostrar su habilidad marcial, instinto de supervivencia y lealtad antes de que se les permita partir hacia el resto de Durotar.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="a91af3",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El Cubil es una cueva excavada en los acantilados aproximadamente en el centro del valle. Alberga a instructores de clase, vendedores y supervisores como Gornek, que orientan a los nuevos reclutas, los equipan y vigilan su progreso durante sus pruebas iniciales.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="b55481",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Los fanáticos pertenecientes al Filo Ardiente han establecido un aquelarre secreto en las cuevas del norte. Aunque los instructores utilizan a sus débiles familiares para poner a prueba a los reclutas, la presencia del culto sugiere que fuerzas sombrías como el Consejo de la Sombra buscan afianzarse justo a las puertas de Durotar.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="1feb80",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Sarkoth es un escórpido venenoso e inusualmente grande que habita en las alturas rocosas del valle. Debido a su agresividad y letalidad, los instructores encargan a los reclutas prometedores que le den caza para poner a prueba su valor y traer su garra destrozada como prueba.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="87bebd",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="16,385,28.558.0,23.490.1,44.300.0,16.231.0,53.276.0,15.251.0",["h"]="6d9866",["n"]="Valle de los Retos",["s"]="Valle de los Retos. Escondido tras los escarpados acantilados rojos del sur de Durotar, el Valle de los Retos sirve como campo de pruebas para los nuevos reclutas de la Horda. Los jóvenes orcos y sus aliados, los trols Lanza Negra, acuden aquí para demostrar su fuerza y ganarse su lugar entre los guerreros de Kalimdor. Aquellos que sobreviven a la implacable fauna del valle y a sus amenazas ocultas parten listos para defender su recién nacida nación. El Valle de los Retos está diseñado para purgar a los débiles antes de que lleguen a poner un pie en las extensiones más amplias de Durotar. Supervisados por cabecillas e instructores apostados en el refugio excavado en la pared del acantilado conocido como El Cubil, los jóvenes combatientes son arrojados al barranco abrasado por el sol para cazar escórpidos, abatir jabalíes agresivos e imponer disciplina entre los peones vagos que talan la escasa madera. La prueba es implacable: quienes demuestran su valía se ganan el derecho a marchar como auténticos soldados de la Horda, mientras que los que fracasan quedan a blanquear bajo el sol del desierto.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Orc"]="The valley represents a rite of passage for every young orc seeking honor, echoing the warrior traditions of Draenor in a newly forged homeland.",["race:Troll"]="Having lost their home on the Echo Isles to Zalazane, the Darkspear trolls train alongside their orc allies in this canyon to earn their place in the Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the traditional proving ground for recruits of the Horde, primarily young orcs and Darkspear trolls. Within its sheltered canyons, new adventurers complete rigorous tasks to demonstrate their martial skill, survival instinct, and loyalty before being permitted to leave for the rest of Durotar.",["al"]={"why are orcs here","what is this place","valley of trials purpose"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Valley of Trials?"},{["a"]="The Den is a cave carved into the cliffs roughly in the center of the valley. It houses class trainers, vendors, and overseers like Gornek who direct new recruits, equip them, and monitor their progress during their initial trials.",["al"]={"the den","cave in valley of trials","who is in the den"},["q"]="What is The Den?"},{["a"]="Cultists belonging to the Burning Blade have established a secret coven in the northern caves. Although trainers use their weak familiars to test recruits, the cult's presence suggests shadowy forces like the Shadow Council are seeking a foothold right on Durotar's doorsteps.",["al"]={"why demons in valley of trials","burning blade in durotar","demons north cave"},["q"]="Why are there demons in a beginner's training ground?"},{["a"]="Sarkoth is an unusually large, venomous scorpid residing in the rocky heights of the valley. Due to his aggression and lethality, instructors task promising recruits with hunting him down to test their courage and bring back his mangled claw as proof.",["al"]={"sarkoth lore","giant scorpid","sarkoth quest"},["q"]="Who is Sarkoth?"}},["kw"]={"burning blade coven","durotar","gornek","orcs","peons","sarkoth","the den","valley of trials"},["n"]="Valley of Trials",["s"]="Tucked away behind the rugged red cliffs of southern Durotar, the Valley of Trials serves as the testing ground for new recruits of the Horde. Young orcs and their Darkspear troll allies come here to prove their strength and earn their place among the warriors of Kalimdor. Those who survive the valley's harsh wildlife and hidden threats depart ready to defend their fledgling nation.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Valley of Trials is designed to weed out the weak before they ever set foot in the broader reaches of Durotar. Overseen by chieftains and trainers stationed in the carved cliffside shelter known as The Den, young fighters are thrust into the sun-scorched gulch to hunt scorpids, culled aggressive boars, and enforce discipline among lazy peons harvesting scarce timber. The trial is uncompromising: those who prove their mettle earn the right to venture forth as true soldiers of the Horde, while those who fail are left to bleach beneath the desert sun.",["t"]="A Crucible of Sand and Stone"},{["b"]="What was once an isolated training ground has recently taken on a far more sinister edge. In the natural caves along the northern cliffs, cultists of the Burning Blade have taken root, summoning minor demonic familiars into the valley. While trainers treat these interlopers as live-combat practice for fresh recruits, the presence of fel magic so close to Orgrimmar's threshold fuels dark rumors that the Shadow Council is actively attempting to sink its claws back into the orcish people.",["t"]="The Shadow in the North"}}}}}
t["subzone:venomweb-vale"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,355,17.469.0,21.590.0,47.285.0,60.264.0,36.143.0,58.241.0",["h"]="e38822",["n"]="Vega Venerácnidas",["s"]="Vega Venerácnidas. Vega Venerácnidas es un valle sombrío en el este de los Claros de Tirisfal, situado justo al sur del Monasterio Escarlata. Antaño un frondoso bosque repleto de caza, la vega ha degenerado en un nido asolado e infestado por arácnidos agresivos y venenosos. Aunque la mayoría de los que pasan por allí lo ignoran, también alberga un antiguo legado como el sagrado lugar de reunión del Consejo de Tirisfal. Antes de que la plaga consumiera Lordaeron, este valle era un remanso de paz con hierba exuberante y árboles verdes, predilecto para los cazadores locales que rastreaban ciervos y conejos. Hoy en día, la podredumbre y una penumbra invasiva dominan el paisaje. Arañas gigantescas y venenosas pululan entre los árboles y las hondonadas, lideradas por el monstruoso arácnido Sri'skulk. El extremo norte de la vega limita con el territorio de la Cruzada Escarlata, donde los canes oscuros merodean cerca del Campamento Escarlata fortificado bajo el mando del teniente Sanders.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, the vale is hallowed ground: it was the historic meeting site of the Council of Tirisfal, where Guardians of old—including Aegwynn—were chosen and empowered.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken travelers traveling toward the Scarlet Monastery must navigate both the lethal toxins of Sri'skulk's brood and the watchful patrols of Lieutenant Sanders's Crusaders to the north."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The spiders are not simply wild beasts or products of the Scourge plague. Centuries ago, a member of the secret Council of Tirisfal magically created and unleashed them in a mad attempt to defend their secluded meeting grounds from trespassers. They multiplied and overtook the valley.",["al"]={"venomweb spiders origin","why so many spiders","who made the spiders"},["q"]="Why are there so many spiders in Venomweb Vale?"},{["a"]="Venomweb Vale served as the traditional secret assembly site for the Council of Tirisfal. Within this quiet valley, elven and human magi gathered to bestow their collective might upon the realm's defenders, including empowering the very first Guardian of Tirisfal.",["al"]={"council of tirisfal vale","guardian meeting place","council history venomweb"},["q"]="What is the Council of Tirisfal's connection to this valley?"},{["a"]="The spider brood is led by a massive, deadly arachnid known as Sri'skulk, who stalks the shadowed hollows beneath the valley's blighted canopy.",["al"]={"spider boss venomweb","sri'skulk","spider leader tirisfal"},["q"]="Who rules the arachnids in the vale?"},{["a"]="Centuries ago, an apprentice named Falric accidentally transformed a boulder into fool's gold during his studies. The strange landmark became the exact meeting point where the famed Guardian Aegwynn would gather with the Council of Tirisfal.",["al"]={"fools gold rock","aegwynn meeting rock","falric gold rock"},["q"]="What is the story behind the fool's gold rock in the vale?"}},["kw"]={"aegwynn","council of tirisfal","falric","lieutenant sanders","scarlet encampment","sri'skulk","tirisfal glades","venomweb vale"},["n"]="Venomweb Vale",["s"]="Venomweb Vale is a shadowed valley in eastern Tirisfal Glades, sitting just south of the Scarlet Monastery. Once a lush woodland teeming with game, the vale has devolved into a blighted nest overrun by aggressive, venomous arachnids. Unknown to most who pass through, it also holds an ancient legacy as the sacred meeting place of the Council of Tirisfal.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the plague consumed Lordaeron, this valley was a peaceful retreat of lush grass and verdant trees, favored by local hunters tracking deer and rabbits. Today, rot and creeping gloom dominate the landscape. Giant, venomous spiders swarm among the trees and hollows, led by the monstrous arachnid Sri'skulk. The vale's northern edge borders the territory of the Scarlet Crusade, where darkhounds prowl near the fortified Scarlet Encampment under Lieutenant Sanders.",["t"]="A Blighted Refuge"},{["b"]="Long before spiders infested the hollows, the vale served as the clandestine gathering ground for the ancient Council of Tirisfal. It was here that the very first Guardian of Tirisfal was empowered to battle demonic incursions. In a desperate and misguided attempt to secure their sanctuary against intruders, one council member bred and unleashed the deadly spiders that plague the basin today. An odd boulder of fool's gold—the result of a centuries-old transmutation mishap by the apprentice Falric—still marks the secluded spot where Guardian Aegwynn once convened with the Council.",["t"]="Legacy of the Council"}}}}}
t["subzone:venture-co-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,280,17.506.0,19.546.1,34.290.0,37.192.0,48.266.0,44.184.0",["h"]="81f0a0",["n"]="Mina de Ventura y Cía",["s"]="Mina de Ventura y Cía. Enclavada en los acantilados orientales de Mulgore, la Mina de Ventura y Cía. es una excavación industrial no autorizada dirigida por codiciosos oportunistas goblins. A pesar de que los tauren les negaron los derechos, Ventura y Cía. excavó en las colinas de todos modos, amenazando el equilibrio natural de las llanuras. Cuando Ventura y Cía. solicitó los derechos para expoliar los minerales de Mulgore, los tauren se negaron en redondo. El cártel corporativo los ignoró, perforando profundamente en la pared montañosa oriental bajo la dirección del Supervisor Saltatuercas. Su extenso complejo cuenta con tres entradas: un túnel a ras de suelo custodiado por matones a sueldo, un mirador en un escarpado acantilado y un pasaje superior que conduce a un pequeño campamento maderero. Las máquinas invasoras, el humo y los montones de escoria representan una profanación flagrante de una tierra sagrada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="Past the mine tunnels and through the higher lumber clearing lurks Twizwick Sprocketgrind, a tinkerer willing to share mechanical trade secrets away from prying corporate eyes.",["race:Tauren"]="The mine is a profound insult to the Earth Mother, bringing soot, noise, and reckless scarring to the ancestral valleys the tribes have sworn to safeguard."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Venture Company sought permission to extract minerals from Mulgore, but the tauren denied their request. Unwilling to respect native territorial claims or environmental balance, the cartel sneaked workers and machinery into the eastern cliffs to plunder the hills without authorization.",["al"]={"why are there goblins here","venture co mulgore reason","who runs the mine"},["q"]="Why are goblins mining in Mulgore?"},{["a"]="Supervisor Fizsprocket oversees all Venture Company operations in Mulgore from his post inside the main entrance. He takes orders directly from the company's executive board and Mogul Razdunk.",["al"]={"mine boss","who leads the mine","supervisor fizsprocket"},["q"]="Who is in charge of this mining site?"},{["a"]="Tauren Outrunners ambushed and set fire to a Venture Company supply caravan near the northern shore of Stonebull Lake to stop machinery from reaching the mine. The goblins swiftly dispatched salvage teams to sift through the charred wreckage and recover their goods.",["al"]={"ravaged caravan story","stonebull lake caravan","who burned the caravan"},["q"]="What happened to the supply caravan by the lake?"},{["a"]="Beyond hollowing out the cliffs for ore, internal communiques reveal plans to construct a lumber mill and deploy shredders to clear-cut Mulgore's trees for additional corporate profit.",["al"]={"venture co plans","goblin shredders mulgore","lumber camp plans"},["q"]="What else do the goblins plan to build here?"}},["kw"]={"fizsprocket","goblins","mulgore","ravaged caravan","razdunk","shredders","stonebull lake","venture co mine"},["n"]="Venture Co. Mine",["s"]="Tucked into the eastern cliffs of Mulgore, the Venture Co. Mine is an unauthorized industrial excavation run by greedy goblin opportunists. Despite being denied rights by the tauren, the Venture Company dug into the hills regardless, threatening the natural balance of the plains.",["sec"]={{["b"]="When the Venture Company sought rights to strip Mulgore of its minerals, the tauren flatly refused. The corporate cartel ignored them, tunneling deep into the eastern mountain wall anyway under the direction of Supervisor Fizsprocket. Their sprawling complex features three entrances—a ground tunnel guarded by hired muscle, a sheer cliffside overlook, and an upper passage leading out to a small lumber camp. The encroaching machines, smoke, and slag heaps represent a blatant defilement of sacred land.",["t"]="Unwanted Industry"},{["b"]="Mining was only the opening bid for the cartel. Internal documents show that Mogul Razdunk and the Venture Company board encouraged Fizsprocket to expand further into full-scale timber harvesting, promising advanced goblin shredders to clear the rolling hills. Although tauren Outrunners attacked and burned a corporate supply caravan near Stonebull Lake to stall their expansion, salvagers were immediately dispatched to recover the cargo. To halt the destruction, the tribes have turned toward direct retaliation against the mine's supervisors.",["t"]="Expanding Ambitions"}}}}}
t["subzone:vul-gol-ogre-mound"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,272,20.578.0,31.517.0,36.171.0,49.266.0,32.239.0,44.227.0,27.151.0",["h"]="54b6cb",["n"]="Túmulo de Vul'Gol",["s"]="Túmulo de Vul'Gol. El Túmulo de Vul'Gol es una cuenca hundida en el sur de Bosque del Ocaso, invadida por los ogros Puñoastillado bajo el mando del bruto Zzarc'Vul. Antaño un grupo de granjas humanas, sus caseríos en ruinas y su caverna subterránea están ahora repletos de cadáveres y del botín saqueado por el clan. Escondido entre las sombras al suroeste de la bifurcación que se dirige hacia la Vega de Tuercespina, el Túmulo de Vul'Gol sirve como sede del clan Puñoastillado en Bosque del Ocaso. La cuenca fue en su día una apacible tierra de cultivo, pero sus habitantes humanos hace tiempo que huyeron o perecieron, dejando tras de sí cabañas destartaladas que ahora reclaman torpes ogros y utilizan como toscos refugios. En el interior de la caverna situada bajo la colina, montones de osos negros degollados dan fe del voraz apetito del clan. Su cacique, Zzarc'Vul, gobierna el campamento, acumulando extrañas baratijas junto a mondanas mercancías desperdiciadas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers traversing the southern path toward Stranglethorn Vale, keeping the Splinter Fist contained at Vul'Gol is vital to maintaining an open supply route through an already treacherous forest.",["race:Human"]="The smashed remnants of farmsteads in the basin are a bitter reminder of how much territory the kingdom of Stormwind has lost in Duskwood over the past generation."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The mound is occupied by the Splinter Fist clan of ogres, led by the hulking chieftain Zzarc'Vul. They dwell among ruined human cottages and deep within an earthen cavern.",["al"]={"who is at vul'gol","vul'gol enemies","ogres in duskwood"},["q"]="Who lives in the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound?"},{["a"]="The Night Watch lacks the manpower to march in force on the southern basin. With Darkshire threatened on all sides by undead, worgen, and the horrors of Addle's Stead, the militia hires travelling adventurers to cull the Splinter Fist instead of risking town guards.",["al"]={"night watch ogres","why doesn't darkshire attack vul'gol"},["q"]="Why hasn't the Night Watch cleared out the ogres?"},{["a"]="Human homesteaders once farmed the fertile pocket in southern Duskwood, back when the region was still known as Brightwood. When the curse fell upon the land, the farms fell to ruin, and the invading ogres claimed the abandoned structures.",["al"]={"ruined buildings vul'gol","vul'gol history"},["q"]="Who lived here before the ogres?"},{["a"]="The Splinter Fist ogres ambushed the hermit Abercrombie and made off with a crate containing his herbs and embalming tools. Unable to fight them himself, Abercrombie directs travelers into the mound to recover his stolen goods.",["al"]={"abercrombie ogres","abercrombie crate"},["q"]="Why did the hermit Abercrombie send me here?"},{["a"]="Vul'Gol lies in the far south of Duskwood, just southwest of the road junction that splits off and leads south toward the border of Stranglethorn Vale.",["al"]={"vul'gol location","how to get to vul'gol"},["q"]="Where is the mound located?"}},["kw"]={"abercrombie","duskwood","night watch","ogres","splinter fist","vul'gol","zzarc'vul"},["n"]="Vul'Gol Ogre Mound",["s"]="Vul'Gol Ogre Mound is a sunken basin in southern Duskwood overrun by the Splinter Fist ogres under the brute Zzarc'Vul. Once a cluster of human homesteads, its ruined farmhouses and subterranean cavern are now littered with the carcasses and scavenged plunder of the clan.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the shadows southwest of the fork heading toward Stranglethorn Vale, the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound serves as the seat of the Splinter Fist clan in Duskwood. The basin was once peaceful farmland, but its human inhabitants have long since fled or perished, leaving behind hollowed-out cabins now claimed by lumbering ogres and used as crude shelters. Inside the cavern beneath the rise, piles of slaughtered black bears attest to the clan's voracious appetite. Their chieftain, Zzarc'Vul, rules over the encampment, hoarding odd trinkets alongside mundane scavenged goods.",["t"]="A Blighted Homestead"},{["b"]="Because the beleaguered Night Watch must stretch its thin ranks to guard Darkshire against rabid worgen and the restless dead, Commander Althea Ebonlocke and her militia rely on outside mercenaries to cull the Splinter Fist numbers before they push north. However, the ogres have made enemies beyond the town guard. They raided the recluse Abercrombie, stealing a crate of his alchemical tools, and attracted the attention of inquisitive mages seeking the arcane lenses that chieftain Zzarc'Vul is rumored to possess.",["t"]="A Menace on the Southern Border"}}}}}
t["subzone:war-quarter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,390,21.477.0,15.390.0,39.237.0,43.313.0,30.216.0,50.196.0",["h"]="0960cf",["n"]="Barrio de la Guerra",["s"]="Barrio de la Guerra. El Barrio de la Guerra es el distrito noroccidental de Entrañas, y sirve como puesto de mando y campo de instrucción marcial para los Renegados. En el interior de sus resonantes salas de piedra, los soldados, sacerdotes y artesanos de Lordaeron perfeccionan sus armas y su Magia de las Sombras en defensa de su incipiente reino. Alberga salas de instrucción para guerreros y sacerdotes junto a maestros de armas e industria pesada. Ocupando el sector noroeste de la metrópolis subterránea, el Barrio de la Guerra se erige como el bastión del poder militar de los Renegados. Bajo sus lúgubres arcos de piedra, guardias de a pie y campeones de élite se reúnen para entrenar en el combate armado. A diferencia de los cuarteles tradicionales de los reinos de los vivos, este centro militar combina la despiadada guerra de hierro con los escalofriantes ritos de las sombras, albergando un siniestro Altar de la Oscuridad donde la disciplina espiritual se funde con la ambición militar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="The War Quarter is your primary haven in the Undercity, offering weapon masters, advanced combat instructors, and heavy armories to prepare you for the brutal frontline battles of Lordaeron.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Housing both training masters and high-heat anvils, the War Quarter is the central hub for smiths hammering out munitions and plate for the Forsaken war effort."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The War Quarter serves as the military headquarters of the Undercity. It hosts martial training grounds for warriors and priests, along with vital crafting centers for blacksmithing and mining to keep the Forsaken army armed and armored.",["al"]={"what is war quarter","war quarter purpose","why visit war quarter"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the War Quarter?"},{["a"]="Forsaken priests largely focus on the discipline of the Shadow, using it as a potent weapon alongside their warriors rather than maintaining pastoral sanctuaries. Their presence near the martial forces and the Altar of Darkness reflects how deeply intertwined faith and warfare are in the defense of the Forsaken.",["al"]={"undead priest location","why are priests in war quarter","priest trainers undercity"},["q"]="Why are priests located in the War Quarter?"},{["a"]="The Altar of Darkness is a focal point of dark spiritual power located within the War Quarter. It is tied to the Forsaken's dark rites and training, anchoring the shadowy magic wielded by their priests and champions.",["al"]={"altar of darkness undercity","altar in war quarter"},["q"]="What is the Altar of Darkness?"},{["a"]="The War Quarter occupies the northwest quadrant of the Undercity's circular layout, northwest of the central Trade Quarter, between the Magic Quarter to the east and the Apothecarium to the south.",["al"]={"where is war quarter","war quarter location","war quarter directions"},["q"]="Where is the War Quarter located in the Undercity?"}},["kw"]={"altar of darkness","barracks","blacksmithing","forsaken","priest trainer","undercity","war quarter","warrior trainer"},["n"]="War Quarter",["s"]="The War Quarter is the northwestern district of the Undercity, serving as the command post and martial training ground for the Forsaken. Within its echoing stone chambers, the soldiers, priests, and crafters of Lordaeron hone their weapons and shadow magic in defense of their fledgling kingdom. It houses training halls for warriors and priests alongside weapon masters and heavy industry.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Occupying the northwest sector of the subterranean metropolis, the War Quarter stands as the bastion of martial strength for the Forsaken. Beneath its gloomy stone arches, rank-and-file guards and elite champions assemble to drill in armed combat. Unlike traditional barracks of living kingdoms, this military center combines ruthless iron warfare with the chilling rites of shadow, housing an ominous Altar of Darkness where spiritual discipline merges with military ambition.",["t"]="The Forsaken Garrison"},{["b"]="Beyond housing warrior and priest guilds, the quarter functions as the heart of Undercity's wartime production. The clatter of blades and armor echoes continually against the stone, supported by the district's blacksmiths, smelters, and weapon masters. Here, iron forged deep in the earth is shaped to outfit the forces defending the ruins of Lordaeron from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade.",["t"]="Forge and Steel"}}}}}
t["subzone:warrior-s-terrace"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,256,19.626.0,45.284.0,50.225.0,24.191.0,55.206.0",["h"]="bdab90",["n"]="Bancal del Guerrero",["s"]="Bancal del Guerrero. El Bancal del Guerrero es el distrito oriental de Darnassus y actúa tanto como núcleo de instrucción marcial como puerta de entrada fortificada de la capital. Con vistas al camino que se adentra en el resto de Teldrassil, alberga a los maestros de batalla de la ciudad, instructores de guerreros y patrullas de Centinelas. Ubicado en el umbral oriental de Darnassus, el Bancal del Guerrero —a veces denominado Sala de la Justicia— se alza como el principal baluarte defensivo frente a las incursiones procedentes de la naturaleza de Teldrassil. Centinelas fuertemente armadas y montadas en sables de la noche custodian sus altas puertas arqueadas, manteniendo una atenta vigilancia sobre los viajeros que llegan. En sus plazas al aire libre, los aspirantes a combatientes se entrenan junto a veteranos curtidos en extensos campos de duelo y galerías de tiro. El distrito también atiende necesidades militares prácticas, albergando a forjadores de armas, armeros y a los maestros de batalla que coordinan a las fuerzas de los elfos de la noche por todo el mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="For warriors training in the night elf capital, this district is your base of operations, providing access to martial instructors, dueling areas, and battlemasters.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The terrace hosts the city's blacksmithing trainers and forge facilities, catering to armor and weapon craft alongside the garrison."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Warrior's Terrace functions as the military heart of Darnassus and its main defensive gateway. It houses the city's martial trainers, battlemasters, dueling grounds, and target ranges, while stationed Sentinels guard the eastern gate leading into the broader boughs of Teldrassil.",["al"]={"what is warrior's terrace","warriors terrace purpose","why warriors terrace"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Warrior's Terrace?"},{["a"]="The grand gates on the eastern edge of the terrace lead directly out of Darnassus and onto the forest paths of greater Teldrassil, connecting the isolated capital to settlement hubs like Dolanaar and Rut'theran Village below.",["al"]={"where does gate go","warriors terrace gate","east gate darnassus"},["q"]="Where does the road through the eastern gate lead?"},{["a"]="The district and its perimeter gates are guarded primarily by the Sentinels, the elite night elven standing army. Many patrol the terraces and gateways while mounted atop armored nightsabers.",["al"]={"who protects warriors terrace","sentinels at warriors terrace","darnassus guards"},["q"]="Who guards the district?"},{["a"]="Bridges and walkways link the Warrior's Terrace directly to the Craftsmen's Terrace to the north, the Tradesmen's Terrace to the south, and the lush Temple Gardens toward the center of the city to the west.",["al"]={"connections warriors terrace","how to get to warriors terrace","what connects to warriors terrace"},["q"]="Which other districts connect to the Warrior's Terrace?"}},["kw"]={"battlemasters","darnassus","dueling grounds","east gate","hall of justice","sentinels","teldrassil","warrior's terrace"},["n"]="Warrior's Terrace",["s"]="The Warrior's Terrace is the eastern district of Darnassus, acting as both a martial training hub and the capital's fortified gateway. Overlooking the road into greater Teldrassil, it houses the city's battlemasters, warrior trainers, and Sentinel patrols.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned at the eastern threshold of Darnassus, the Warrior's Terrace—sometimes referred to as the Hall of Justice—stands as the primary defensive bulwark against incursions from the Teldrassil wilds. Heavily armed Sentinels mounted on nightsabers guard its high arched gates, maintaining a vigilant watch over incoming travelers. Within its open-air plazas, aspiring combatants drill alongside seasoned veterans on extensive dueling grounds and target ranges. The district also serves practical military needs, hosting weapon smiths, armorers, and the battlemasters coordinating night elf forces across the wider world.",["t"]="Shield of Darnassus"}}}}}
t["subzone:warsong-labor-camp"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,280,20.518.0,20.390.0,40.113.0,33.189.0,36.258.0,40.223.0",["h"]="f4684e",["n"]="Campo de trabajos forzados Grito de Guerra",["s"]="Campo de trabajos forzados Grito de Guerra. El Campo de trabajos forzados Grito de Guerra es un puesto de tala aislado de la Horda escondido en el sureste de Vallefresno. Operado por leñadores Grito de Guerra y defendido por centinelas orcos, el campamento de trabajo tala madera para impulsar el crecimiento de Durotar mientras desafía la hostilidad del bosque circundante. Situado al este del Lago Cielo Estrellado y al suroeste de El Túmulo de Dor'danil, el Campo de trabajos forzados Grito de Guerra existe con un único propósito vital: talar la densa madera de Vallefresno. Las secas llanuras de Durotar ofrecen poca madera utilizable para construir ciudades como Orgrimmar, lo que obliga al clan Grito de Guerra a adentrarse en los disputados bosques. Con una dotación de recios leñadores y guardias orcos, el lugar opera en un relativo aislamiento, talando árboles milenarios a pesar de la constante amenaza de los exploradores elfos de la noche y las partidas de guerra de la Alianza que cruzan la zona.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The lumber harvested by these loggers is crucial to building and maintaining Orgrimmar, making their remote work station a vital economic lifeline in contested territory.",["race:NightElf"]="The camp represents a continuous wound in the living woods of Ashenvale, deforesting ancestral groves to fuel the warmachine of Durotar."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The labor camp lies in southeastern Ashenvale, east of Fallen Sky Lake and southwest of the Dor'Danil Barrow Den.",["al"]={"warsong labor camp location","where is warsong labor camp","finding labor camp"},["q"]="Where is the Warsong Labor Camp located?"},{["a"]="The outpost serves as a timber harvesting operation. Orc loggers cut and process the ancient woods of Ashenvale to provide building materials for Orgrimmar and other settlements in Durotar.",["al"]={"why are orcs here","what do they do here","warsong logging camp purpose"},["q"]="What is the purpose of this camp?"},{["a"]="The camp sits in isolation, far from major Horde fortifications. Night elves fiercely despise the harvesting of their sacred forests, and Alliance champions often raid the outpost because its remote position prevents nearby guards from offering swift backup.",["al"]={"alliance attacks labor camp","why is it targeted","is the camp safe"},["q"]="Why is the camp frequently attacked?"},{["a"]="Warchief Thrall originally sent Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan into Ashenvale during the Third War specifically to harvest lumber. The Labor Camp stands as an active continuation of those original logging efforts.",["al"]={"did grom make this","grom hellscream labor camp","history of the camp"},["q"]="Did Grommash Hellscream found this camp?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","dor'danil","fallen sky lake","labor camp","loggers","lumber","timber","warsong"},["n"]="Warsong Labor Camp",["s"]="The Warsong Labor Camp is an isolated Horde timber-harvesting outpost tucked away in southeastern Ashenvale. Operated by Warsong loggers and defended by orcish sentries, the work site cuts lumber to fuel the growth of Durotar while braving the hostility of the surrounding forest.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated east of Fallen Sky Lake and southwest of the Dor'Danil Barrow Den, the Warsong Labor Camp exists for one vital purpose: harvesting the dense timber of Ashenvale. The dry plains of Durotar offer little usable lumber to build cities like Orgrimmar, forcing the Warsong clan to push deep into the contested woods. Staffed by hardy loggers and orcish guards, the site operates in relative isolation, grinding through ancient trees despite the ever-present threat of night elf scouts and passing Alliance warbands.",["t"]="Timber for the Horde"},{["b"]="Because of its remote location far from the main road and fortified bases like Splintertree Post, the camp is exceptionally vulnerable. Alliance raiders often strike the working peons and watchmen, knowing reinforcements will not arrive swiftly. To the night elves, every felled tree is an act of sacrilege, turning this mundane logging camp into a perennial flashpoint in the regional war.",["t"]="A Vulnerable Outpost"}}}}}
t["subzone:warsong-lumber-camp"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,433,20.678.0,15.661.0,38.357.0,23.276.0,48.307.0,38.272.0",["h"]="4a9b89",["n"]="Aserradero Grito de Guerra",["s"]="Aserradero Grito de Guerra. El Aserradero Grito de Guerra es una explotación maderera orca fortificada en las profundidades de Vallefresno, dirigida por el clan Grito de Guerra para talar madera destinada a la Horda. Respaldado por el fortificado Fuerte de Kargathia, sirve tanto de salvavidas económico para los asentamientos cercanos de la Horda como de constante provocación para los elfos de la noche. El sonido incesante de las trituradoras de manufactura goblin desgarrando ramas milenarias convierte este claro en un punto crítico de la guerra forestal. Tallado directamente bajo la densa cubierta forestal del este de Vallefresno, el Aserradero Grito de Guerra es el motor industrial que impulsa la expansión de la Horda por Kalimdor. Los peones orcos y los ingenieros goblin contratados despojan el bosque con el zumbido de sus trituradoras, transformando troncos imponentes en madera con la que reforzar las murallas de puestos de avanzada como el cercano Puesto del Hachazo y consolidar la incipiente nación de Durotar. El campamento está fuertemente fortificado contra los constantes contraataques de los elfos de la noche, articulándose en torno a las empalizadas del Fuerte de Kargathia y una activa perrera para los feroces lobos de guerra del clan. Para los Grito de Guerra, cada árbol talado significa supervivencia y fuerza; para las Centinelas nativas, cada hoja de sierra es un acto de sacrilegio.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The lumber harvested here supplies the building materials for Splintertree Post and the fortifications safeguarding the Horde's future across Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="The camp's whining shredders and falling trees represent a direct, brutal assault on the sacred balance of Ashenvale that the Sentinels have vowed to extinguish."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The lands settled by the Horde—particularly Durotar and the Barrens—are arid and sparse, lacking the dense timber required to construct buildings, palisades, and war machinery. Ashenvale offers a massive, virtually endless supply of prime wood essential for the survival and expansion of orc outposts like Splintertree Post and the capital of Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"why cut trees","warsong logging reasons","why does horde need wood"},["q"]="Why is the Horde logging in Ashenvale?"},{["a"]="Kargathia Keep is the fortified stronghold anchoring the Warsong Lumber Camp. It provides barracks, strategic command, and a reinforced bastion where peons and overseers can retreat and hold off night elf ambushes when Sentinels or local wildlife strike the logging perimeter.",["al"]={"kargathia keep purpose","fort in lumber camp","warsong keep ashenvale"},["q"]="What is Kargathia Keep?"},{["a"]="To the night elves, Ashenvale is a sacred ancestral homeland protected by nature spirits and ancients. Felling ancient trees with noisy, smoke-belching goblin machinery is considered wanton destruction and outright desecration, prompting constant guerrilla attacks to expel the Warsong orcs from the forest.",["al"]={"night elf reaction","why elves attack lumber camp","sentinel attacks"},["q"]="Why are the night elves so hostile to this camp?"},{["a"]="Goblin mercenaries and technicians provide the specialized technology driving the lumber operation, most notably steam-powered shredders. These machines allow the Warsong clan to harvest and strip massive ancient trees at speeds conventional hand axes could never achieve.",["al"]={"goblins at warsong camp","why are shredders here","goblin machinery ashenvale"},["q"]="What role do goblins play in the camp?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","kargathia keep","shredders","splintertree post","timber","warsong clan","warsong lumber camp"},["n"]="Warsong Lumber Camp",["s"]="The Warsong Lumber Camp is a fortified orc logging operation deep in Ashenvale, run by the Warsong clan to harvest timber for the Horde. Anchored by the fortified Kargathia Keep, it stands as both an economic lifeline for nearby Horde settlements and an unrelenting provocation to the night elves. The constant sound of goblin-built shredders chewing through ancient boughs makes this clearing a primary flashpoint of the forest war.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved straight out of the dense canopy of eastern Ashenvale, the Warsong Lumber Camp is the industrial engine fueling the Horde's expansion across Kalimdor. Orc peons and hired goblin engineers strip the forest with whirring shredders, processing towering trunks into lumber to reinforce outpost walls like nearby Splintertree Post and build up the fledgling nation of Durotar. The camp is heavily fortified against constant night elf counterattacks, centering on the stockades of Kargathia Keep and an active kennel for the clan's fierce war wolves. For the Warsong, every felled tree is survival and strength; for the native Sentinels, every saw blade is an act of sacrilege.",["t"]="Heart of the Harvest"},{["b"]="The Warsong clan's presence in these woods dates back to the Third War, when Grom Hellscream first led his warriors into the sacred groves to claim wood for the Horde. That initial deforestation ignited the fury of the demigod Cenarius and brought down the ancient wrath of the night elves. Though the modern camp operates under the banners of Thrall's Horde, the old animosities burn just as fiercely. Surrounded by untamed timber, hostile elves, and the lingering demonic corruption around neighboring Felfire Hill, the camp's defenders remain armed around the clock, harvesting trees with axes in hand and ready to drop their timber to repel the next ambush.",["t"]="A Legacy of War"}}}}}
t["subzone:weathered-nook"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,319,19.505.0,36.227.0,32.191.0,48.189.0",["h"]="1db951",["n"]="El Hueco Perdido",["s"]="El Hueco Perdido. Escondido a lo largo del acantilado norte de Las Mil Agujas, El Hueco Perdido es una hendidura y refugio apartado situado muy por encima del fondo del cañón. Con vistas al vasto mar de agujas de piedra, sirve de modesto hogar y retiro para tauren solitarios que buscan la contemplación tranquila lejos de los bulliciosos asentamientos. Esculpido en la escarpada pared de arenisca al norte de Poblado Viento Libre, los viajeros que recorren la cuenca del cañón pueden pasar por alto El Hueco Perdido con facilidad. Una rampa natural serpentea por la pared del acantilado y conduce a una cornisa resguardada y a una cueva al abrigo de los vientos dominantes. En lugar de albergar un puesto militar o un gran asentamiento, el rincón sirve como un humilde hogar para caminantes solitarios como Dorn Acechaprados y Prate Nubeprofeta, ofreciendo seguridad, aislamiento y una vista panorámica de las mesetas azotadas por el viento.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Horde wanderers exploring the heights of the canyon walls will find friendly kindred sheltering here along the northern cliffs.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, the Weathered Nook represents the quiet spirit of self-reliance, offering a peaceful vantage point across the canyon to commune with the elements away from the busy bridges of Freewind Post."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The nook is nestled along the northern cliff wall of Thousand Needles. From Freewind Post, travel north until you reach the towering rock face, then follow the cliffs east until you find a winding ramp leading up the mesa wall.",["al"]={"how to find weathered nook","weathered nook location","where is nook"},["q"]="Where is the Weathered Nook located?"},{["a"]="The shelter is home to Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer, solitary tauren who have chosen this remote ledge above the canyon rather than dwelling atop the crowded towers of Freewind Post.",["al"]={"who is here","weathered nook residents","npcs in nook"},["q"]="Who lives in the Weathered Nook?"},{["a"]="While the residents are tauren and align naturally with their kindred, the nook is not a formal Horde garrison. It is a humble personal camp and dwelling tucked quietly into the wilderness.",["al"]={"is this a horde camp","horde weathered nook"},["q"]="Is the Weathered Nook affiliated with the Horde?"}},["kw"]={"cave","cliff","dorn plainstalker","freewind post","prate cloudseer","thousand needles","weathered nook"},["n"]="Weathered Nook",["s"]="Tucked away along the northern cliffside of Thousand Needles, the Weathered Nook is a secluded cleft and shelter perched high above the canyon floor. Overlooking the vast sea of stone spires, it serves as a modest home and retreat for solitary tauren dwellers seeking quiet contemplation away from bustling settlements.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the sheer sandstone wall north of Freewind Post, the Weathered Nook is easily missed by travelers passing along the canyon basin below. A natural ramp winds up the cliff face, leading to a sheltered ledge and cave out of the prevailing winds. Rather than housing a military outpost or large settlement, the nook serves as a humble homestead for solitary wanderers like Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer, offering safety, seclusion, and a sweeping view across the windswept needle plateaus.",["t"]="Haven on the Cliffs"}}}}}
